      "narrative": "Cellino is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Nabiha Saklayen and Marinna Madrid, operating within a sector encompassing 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 identifiable private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nGiven the absence of sufficiently narrow peer multiples\u2014the biotech & health sector yielded no same-stage comparable triplets meeting statistical thresholds\u2014and the lack of disclosed revenue for a private-stage target, only stage-progression methodology proved applicable. Using total capital raised of $125M as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier standard for Series A advancement yields an implied valuation of $250M. Public sector medians (6.6x P/S across the three comps) remain unusable without target revenue disclosure, a common constraint in pre-revenue or early-stage private biotech.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $212M to $288M, centered on $250M. This single-method triangulation carries material uncertainty around stage-appropriate step-up multiples and the applicability of raised capital as a valuation anchor in early-stage biotech, where capital efficiency and clinical-stage milestones typically drive value more directly than deployment. Refinement would require either peer multiples from a larger comparable set or disclosed revenue and margin trajectory data.",
