      "narrative": "Phaidra is a Series B AI & Software company founded by Jim Gao (ex-Google DeepMind, led industrial AI programs including data center cooling optimization), Vedavyas Panneershelvam (primary engineer on AlphaGo), and Katherine Hoffman (ex-Trane, Raytheon). The company has raised $120M to date. The valuation peer set comprises 3 same-sector, same-stage private comparables\u2014Scale AI ($29.0B), Physical Intelligence ($5.6B), and Black Forest Labs ($3.2B)\u2014alongside 1 public comparable (Palantir, PLTR) and 5 additional private references.\n\nTwo valuation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis, using the $120M total raised as a proxy base and applying a typical 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, yields $228M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 direct comparables produces $5.6B, reflecting the median of a $3.2B\u2013$29.0B range. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneity in AI software company maturity and go-to-market traction at Series B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $194M (low) to $6.4B (high), with a median of $2.9B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around whether Phaidra's market position and technical capabilities align with the lower end (Physical Intelligence, Black Forest Labs) or the upper tier (Scale AI). Key uncertainties include revenue and customer concentration, product-market fit evidence, and the monetization pathway for the core industrial AI application.",
