      "narrative": "Smack Technologies is a Series A-stage defense and security company founded by Andy Markoff (former MARSOC, ex-Palantir) and Clint Alanis (20+ years Marine special ops). The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 3 same-sector, same-stage private peers (Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI) plus a broader comp set of 8 private firms and 2 public companies in defense tech.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $32M in total capital raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a $64M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 directly comparable Series A companies yields a median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous market positioning and growth trajectories within frontier defense tech.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $54M to $460M, with a median of $232M. The stage-progression method produces the lower bound, reflecting a conservative discount to peer medians. The peer-median approach anchors the upper bound but exhibits substantial internal variance\u2014the $3.9B spread between NODA AI and Stark Defence underscores difficulty in identifying truly fungible comparables. Key uncertainties include commercial traction (not provided), competitive positioning relative to Anduril and Helsing, and whether Markoff's Palantir background signals defensible IP or market access.",
