      "narrative": "Phoenix Tailings is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Nick Myers (CEO) and Tom\u00e1s Villal\u00f3n (CTO, Activate Boston fellow) that has raised $117.8M to date. The valuation framework incorporates a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (LNZA), including KoBold Metals ($3.0B, Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B, Series C), and Amogy ($700M, Series C).\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement to the $118M raised proxy, yielding $224M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a $1.0B implied value, with the full peer range spanning $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulation of both methods supports a valuation range of $190M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $612M. The wide spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around Phoenix Tailings' relative maturity and technical de-risking versus the peer set. Stage-progression skews conservative given the company's Series B status; peer multiples reflect the scale achieved by later-stage comparable companies. Key uncertainties include commercialization timeline, capital efficiency relative to peers, and near-term funding environment for climate-tech sector participants.",
