      "narrative": "CX2 Industries is a Series A-stage defense and security company founded by Nathan Mintz and Porter Smith that has raised $46M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of 10 private peers and 2 public comparables in the defense & security sector, including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing among private companies, alongside public peers DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo methods were applied to triangulate enterprise value. The stage-progression method uses the $46M raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage progression, yielding $92M. The peer-median method examines three same-stage, same-sector comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M)\u2014producing a median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a low of $78M, a median of $246M, and a high of $460M. The median reflects material uncertainty around the appropriate comp set weighting: the peer universe exhibits substantial dispersion, and the stage-progression method relies heavily on whether total raised accurately proxies pre-money valuation at entry. The wide range ($78M\u2013$460M) suggests that CX2's specific technology maturity, customer traction, and defensibility relative to the peer set warrant deeper diligence before settling on a point estimate.",
