      "narrative": "Skydio, a Series F autonomous systems company in Defense & Security, carries a current post-money valuation of $4.4B following $825M+ in cumulative fundraising. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 18 same-sector comparable companies, supplemented by two public defense technology comps (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and eight private peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo quantitative methods inform the valuation range. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.3x step-up multiplier to the $4.4B Series F post-money, implying $5.7B at the next financing stage. Peer-median analysis across 18 Defense & Security comparables yields a median valuation of $2.4B, with observed range from $1.0B floor to $18.0B ceiling (exemplified by outliers Helsing at $18.0B and Shield AI at $12.7B). The divergence between peer median and stage-progression reflects heterogeneity in the defense technology cohort and valuation dispersion typical at later stages.\n\nTriangulation of both methods supports a valuation range of $2.0B to $6.6B, with a median of $4.0B. The current $4.4B valuation sits modestly above the calculated median, positioning Skydio at the high end of this range. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate relative to peers and the sustainability of valuations in a sector exhibiting substantial spread ($1.0B\u2013$18.0B), suggesting material variance in market perception of growth and defensibility across Defense & Security companies.",
