      "narrative": "Mach Industries is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Ethan Thornton that has raised $185M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms\u2014all operating in the Defense & Security sector at similar stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $185M total raised as a baseline and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implying a valuation of $352M. The peer-median approach references 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables including Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), yielding a median valuation of $1.0B against a range of $300M to $3.0B.\n\nReconciling both methods produces a triangulated range of $299M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $676M. The stage-progression method anchors toward the lower bound given reliance on historical funding as a proxy, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher valuations. The wide spread reflects material heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014particularly the $3.0B outlier\u2014and limited visibility into relative product maturity, revenue traction, and customer concentration. Key uncertainties include Mach's revenue run-rate, customer diversification versus government concentration, and capital efficiency versus the peer cohort.",
