      "narrative": "Radiant, a Series D nuclear energy company founded by Doug Bernauer, has raised $465M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 9 peers\u20143 public (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 6 private (including Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy)\u2014though the private nuclear energy financing market remains sparse at comparable stages and scales.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable framework. Using Radiant's last post-money valuation of $1.0B as the base and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement yields $1.5B. The peer-median approach is not viable here: while 5 nuclear energy peers exist in the broader market, none satisfy narrow filtering criteria (same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier) at sufficient density. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material bias given nuclear energy's distinct risk and capital profiles.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.7B, with a median point of $1.5B. This range reflects primarily the stage-progression signal. Key uncertainties include technology and regulatory de-risking between Series D and the next funding round, and the absence of sufficiently granular private market comparables in nuclear energy at this valuation tier to validate or adjust the stage-based estimate.",
