      "narrative": "X-Energy, a nuclear energy company at IPO stage led by founder Kam Ghaffarian, presents a valuation challenge due to limited comparable data. The analysis draws from a sector comp universe of 8 nuclear energy peers: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 5 private-stage firms (Oklo, Valar Atomics, Nano Nuclear Energy, Fuse Energy, Deep Fission). X-Energy has raised $1.1B+ to date and carries a current valuation of $5.64B.\n\nThe peer-median approach proved inapplicable here. The nuclear energy sector contains only 4 same-sector peers overall, but filtering for matching stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier yielded fewer than the three datapoints required for statistical reliability. Restricting analysis to same-stage IPO candidates or valuation-tier peers produced insufficient observations; broadening to all-sector medians would introduce significant comparability noise given the heterogeneous business models and development timelines within nuclear energy.\n\nGiven data constraints, the analysis cannot triangulate to a supported range through traditional multiples approaches. The valuation of $5.64B should be stress-tested against public market entry conditions for OKLO, NNE, and SMR, but direct peer multiples remain unreliable. Key uncertainties center on regulatory pathway clarity, capital intensity trajectory, and whether the private comp set meaningfully anchors value at IPO. Additional disclosure of peer-specific revenue, EBITDA, or stage-specific funding rounds would strengthen triangulation.",
