      "narrative": "Relativity Space is a private-stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised $1.335B to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, Impulse Space, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nStandard triangulation methods are constrained by data limitations. Peer-median valuation cannot be applied: while 14 same-sector peers exist, only 1 operates at Relativity's stage, and filtering for adjacent-stage or similar-valuation-tier peers yields fewer than the 3 minimum datapoints required for statistical confidence. Public-comp anchoring is similarly inapplicable because Relativity's revenue is not disclosed\u2014a typical limitation for private companies\u2014and applying the Space & Aerospace public median P/S of 27.4x would rest on an unmeasurable foundation.\n\nGiven these constraints, the analysis cannot produce a narrow valuation range grounded in quantitative triangulation. The $1.335B capital raised establishes a floor for cumulative investor commitment but does not directly imply current fair value. Meaningful valuation would require either Relativity's revenue or EBITDA figures, or an expansion of the same-stage private comparable set. Key uncertainties include the company's revenue scale relative to peers, margin trajectory, and execution risk in a capital-intensive sector. Further analysis should prioritize obtaining either target financials or same-stage comp data.",
