      "narrative": "Palantir operates in the AI & Software sector as a publicly traded company with a current market capitalization of $312.5 billion following its transition from private markets, where it raised over $3 billion pre-IPO. The peer universe for valuation purposes is constrained: the AI & Software sector contains 15 total comparables, but only 1 public peer (PLTR itself) and 8 identifiable private peers, including Waymo, Figure AI, Scale AI, Reflection AI, and Applied Intuition. This fragmented comp set reflects the heterogeneity of AI-focused businesses across different applications and revenue models.\n\nTraditional peer-median analysis is not applicable here. The narrow filters required for methodological rigor\u2014same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier peers\u2014yielded fewer than three datapoints, the minimum threshold for meaningful triangulation. A fallback to the full 15-company sector median would introduce material bias given the wide dispersion of business models, maturity levels, and revenue profiles within AI & Software. This limitation forces reliance on transaction multiples, discounted cash flow analysis, or qualitative assessment frameworks rather than comparable-company analysis.\n\nGiven these constraints, any valuation conclusion must acknowledge the analytical boundary: the current $312.5 billion market price reflects public market sentiment and liquidity, but establishing an independent valuation range through peer triangulation is not supported by the available data. Uncertainty around appropriate discount rates, revenue growth trajectories, and margin sustainability remains unresolved by comparable-company methodology alone.",
