      "narrative": "Amca is a robotics and manufacturing company at the IPO stage, founded by Jai Malik and Eli Giovanetti, having raised $76.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine peers: one public company (ticker 277810.KQ) and eight private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, and Bedrock Robotics.\n\nThe peer-median method proved inapplicable to this valuation. While ten same-sector peers exist in Robotics & Manufacturing, the narrow filtering criteria\u2014same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier\u2014yielded fewer than three datapoints in any category. Applying an all-sector median would introduce substantial noise and misrepresent the company's position relative to truly comparable businesses. This constraint reflects the fragmented nature of private robotics financing and the absence of a cohesive peer cohort at Amca's IPO juncture.\n\nGiven these data limitations, a definitive triangulated valuation range cannot be responsibly derived from the current peer set. The analysis identifies a material gap: robust valuation support requires either (1) expansion of the comp set to include later-stage or earlier-stage robotics businesses with disclosed valuations, or (2) application of revenue or earnings multiples if such metrics are available for Amca and peers. Until comparable datapoints reach a sufficient density, investors should treat any single-method valuation estimate as provisional and flag stage and sector-specific execution risk as a key uncertainty.",
