      "narrative": "Retro Biosciences is a Series A biotech company founded by Joe Betts-LaCroix that has raised $180M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 3 public peers in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies including Colossal Biosciences, Recursion Pharmaceuticals, and Freenome, though the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage clustering for reliable median-based triangulation.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method here. Using total capital raised ($180M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $3.6B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Retro's revenue is not disclosed, and peer-median comparison is not feasible given only one adjacent-stage comparable in the narrow peer set. The median and base case therefore rest entirely on stage progression.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $3.1B to $4.1B, with $3.6B as the central estimate. This range reflects sensitivity around the stage-progression multiplier rather than independent method validation. Key uncertainties are Retro's undisclosed revenue run rate (which would enable public-comp anchoring), fundraising terms and preference structure from the $180M raised, and the heterogeneity of pipeline and clinical-stage risk across the private peer group. A more robust triangulation would require either disclosed financials or access to narrower peer valuations.",
