      "narrative": "Atom Bodies is a Series A biotech company founded by Tyler Hayes, Doug Satzger, and Eric Monsef that has raised $142.2M to date. The valuation exercise draws on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage biotech companies including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable given available data. Stage-progression analysis uses the $142.2M total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage advancement, yielding $284M. This method is grounded in the empirical observation that biotech companies at Atom Bodies' development phase commonly achieve 2x valuation expansion between early institutional funding and later rounds. Public-comp anchoring using a 6.6x median price-to-sales multiple across the three public peers cannot be applied without the target's revenue figure, which private companies typically do not disclose. Peer-median analysis was not feasible; while 7 same-sector peers exist, the narrow filtering criteria (same stage, adjacent stage, or comparable valuation tier) returned insufficient datapoints for statistical reliability.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $242M to $327M, centered on $284M, derived entirely from stage-progression mechanics. Key uncertainties include the appropriate exit multiplier for this specific sector and subsegment within biotech, the timing and terms of the next fundraising event, and Atom Bodies' relative competitive positioning versus named peers.",
