      "narrative": "Claros is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Daniel Kultran and Grant Verstandig. The company has raised $30M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector comprises 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (LNZA); however, the peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comps with similar valuation tiers to support a robust peer-median analysis.\n\nThe primary valuation method applied is Stage-Progression, which uses the $30M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement. This yields an implied post-money valuation of $75M. A sensitivity band around this central estimate\u2014accounting for variance in step-up timing and magnitude\u2014produces a low of $64M and a high of $86M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $64M\u2013$86M, with a median point of $75M. This estimate rests entirely on stage-progression mechanics and carries meaningful uncertainty around the appropriate multiplier, capital efficiency relative to sector norms, and time-to-next-funding event. Absent a sufficiently deep peer dataset, future rounds should be reassessed against emerging comparable transactions in frontier energy technologies.",
