      "narrative": "Forterra, founded by Alberto Lacaze, is a Series B-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $228M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms operating in the same sector and stage. The private peer set includes Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns, among others.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $228M total raised as a proxy baseline, applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $433M. The Peer-Median method benchmarks against 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables, which exhibit a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B. This reflects meaningful dispersion in the peer cohort, likely attributable to differences in revenue traction, technology maturity, and customer concentration.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $368M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median point of $717M. The wide spread\u2014a 3.1x delta between low and high\u2014reflects material uncertainty around Forterra's relative position within the peer set. Key drivers of variance include burn rate relative to raised capital, customer acquisition and retention metrics, and the competitive intensity within Defense & Security at this stage. Further diligence on unit economics and customer concentration would narrow this range materially.",
