      "narrative": "Firehawk Aerospace is a Series A-stage defense & security company that has raised $25M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public and 8 private\u2014spanning the same sector and stage, including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $25M total raised as a base proxy and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $50M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M). The median of this set is $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B. The wide range reflects meaningful heterogeneity in capital intensity and market positioning within the Defense & Security frontier-tech segment.\n\nTriangulating across both methods produces a valuation range of $42M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $225M. The gap between stage-progression ($50M) and peer-median ($400M) reflects uncertainty around Firehawk's relative position within a sector marked by high dispersion. Key sensitivities include the comparability of peer capital efficiency, the pace of product commercialization, and customer concentration in what remains an early-stage, defense-dependent market.",
