      "narrative": "Axiom Space, a Series G space infrastructure company founded by Michael T. Suffredini and Kam Ghaffarian, operates within a sector populated by 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX and Rocket Lab. The company has raised $350M to date.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the Stage-Progression method is applicable. Using total capital raised ($350M) as a valuation proxy, a 1.25x step-up multiplier typical for Series G advancement yields $219M. Peer-Median analysis was not viable\u2014while 14 same-sector private companies exist, none yielded sufficient comparable data points at identical or adjacent stages and valuation tiers. Public-Comp Anchoring could not be applied; the Space & Aerospace sector median trading multiple stands at 27.4x across five public names, but Axiom Space's revenue is not disclosed, precluding meaningful application of this method.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $186M to $252M, with a median of $219M. This reflects meaningful uncertainty inherent in the analysis: reliance on a single methodology, lack of granular private-market comparables at Series G stage, and absence of target-level financials. The median should be treated as directional rather than precise. Key unknowns affecting valuation include contract backlog, capital efficiency trajectory, and competitive positioning relative to the identified peer set.",
