      "narrative": "Apptronik is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $935M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private firms and one public entity across the robotics sector, including adjacent-stage peers such as Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base of $100M and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $200M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector comparables\u2014spanning Series B and Seed stages with valuations between $1.1B and $2.0B\u2014yields a median of $1.7B. The divergence between methods reflects the substantial stage and maturity variance within the peer set.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $170M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $950M. The wide band reflects material uncertainty around (1) where within the peer cohort Apptronik's operational traction most closely aligns, and (2) whether the company's stage and capital efficiency justify positioning toward the lower or upper portion of comparables. Further clarity on revenue, customer traction, and burn rate would narrow this range materially.",
