      "narrative": "Atomic Industries is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Aaron Slodov, Austin Bishop, and Lou Young Jr., having raised $25M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 9 comparable companies spanning robotics and adjacent manufacturing automation, including 8 private firms (Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and others) and 1 public benchmark.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $25M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A forward, implies a valuation of $50M. Peer-median analysis leverages four same-sector comparables at Series B and Seed stages\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B)\u2014yielding a median of $1.7B with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range of $42.5M to $2.0B, with a median of $875M. This dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty inherent in early-stage robotics valuations, where stage-progression conservatism conflicts sharply with peer-based upside assumptions. The peer median assumes Atomic will reach Series B scale and performance parity; the stage-progression figure assumes more modest near-term dilution. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to sampled peers, technical validation progress, and whether robotics/manufacturing subsectors will sustain current public and private multiples.",
