      "narrative": "Diode, a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company led by Davide Asnaghi and Lenny Khazan, has raised $10M+ to date. The valuation framework references a comp universe of 1 public company (ticker 277810.KQ) and 8 private peers including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI operating in the same sector.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method given data constraints. Using the $10M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical Seed-to-next-stage multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $25M. A peer-median approach is not viable; while 10 same-sector robotics companies exist in the reference set, fewer than three comparable companies meet narrow filters for stage, timing, or valuation tier, rendering sector-wide medians uninformative.\n\nThe triangulated range derived from available methods is $21M (low) to $29M (high), with a median of $25M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single applicable method rather than convergence across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 2.5x multiplier for Diode's specific risk profile and the absence of direct peer data at identical stage and valuation scale. Refinement would require either a larger cohort of directly comparable private Seed-stage robotics companies or additional financial metrics from the target.",
