      "narrative": "Quilter is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Sergiy Nesterenko that has raised $15M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics), supplemented by a broader comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public equity comparable.\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($15M) as a proxy for post-money valuation, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression, yielding $30M. Peer-median analysis across the four-company comparable set produces a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The latter reflects both Seed-stage (Walden Robotics at $1.1B) and Series B pricing (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity at $1.8B\u2013$2.0B).\n\nTriangulation of these two methods produces a wide range: $26M (low), $865M (median), and $2.0B (high). The disparity reflects the stage and valuation heterogeneity within the peer set. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively to capital deployed; the peer-median captures market-clearing prices for later-stage robotics companies but may overstate Quilter's value given earlier stage. Material uncertainties include unit economics, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether the peer set adequately reflects frontier-tech execution risk at earlier stages.",
