      "narrative": "Solugen, a Series D climate and energy technology company that has raised $640M+, is evaluated against a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies: Redwood Materials ($6.0B Series D), KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, implies $960M. Peer-median analysis across the four-company climate and energy cohort yields a $2.0B median valuation, with a range of $700M to $6.0B. These methods triangulate to a low of $816M, median of $1.5B, and high of $2.3B.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $816M\u2013$2.3B, with a midpoint of $1.5B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations (nearly 9x spread from floor to ceiling) and limited sample size, both reflecting significant heterogeneity in capital intensity, revenue stage, and technology maturity across the climate-tech sector. The peer median substantially exceeds the stage-progression method, suggesting either that Solugen's operational or financial metrics lag peer performance or that recent market dynamics have compressed valuations relative to earlier fundraises in the comparison set.",
