      "narrative": "fab2 is a seed-stage chip design company founded by Jim Keller and Sam Zeloof, operating in a competitive sector populated by 3 public comps (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched. The company has raised $15M+ to date.\n\nStage-progression analysis provides the primary valuation anchor. Using the $15M total raised as a proxy for seed-stage value and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement yields $38M. This method is applicable given the company's clear stage positioning, though it relies on raised capital as a proxy rather than post-money valuation. Peer-median analysis is not feasible: while 12 same-sector peers exist, insufficient overlap exists on stage and valuation tier to support a statistically reliable median (minimum of 3 required). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 21.5x across Semiconductors) cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures, which private companies rarely provide.\n\nThe triangulation range is $32M\u2013$43M, with a median of $38M. This range reflects modest variance bounds (\u00b115%) around the single applicable method rather than true method diversity. Key uncertainties include the actual post-money valuation at fab2's most recent funding round, which would refine the base; competitive positioning relative to the named peer set; and technology differentiation vis-\u00e0-vis both established public chipmakers and well-funded private competitors. Additional disclosure of revenue run rate or near-term commercialization milestones would enable public-comp validation.",
