      "narrative": "Kodiak AI is a Series C-stage defense and security company that has raised $250M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 13 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies, comprising 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including Helsing, Saronic, Quantum-Systems, Chaos Industries, and Dream Security.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the $250M total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $425M. The peer-median method benchmarks against the 13-company cohort, which exhibits a median valuation of $2.1B (range: $300M\u2013$18.0B). The peer sample includes Series D outliers at $18.0B and $9.2B alongside Series C and earlier-stage companies at $8.0B, $3.0B, and lower.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $361M (low) to $2.5B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in the peer set, particularly the influence of high-valuation outliers (Helsing, Saronic, Quantum-Systems). Key uncertainties include stage-adjusted positioning relative to top-quartile peers and whether Kodiak's operational metrics and customer traction warrant valuation toward the peer median or the lower stage-progression estimate. Further diligence on revenue, customer concentration, and technology defensibility would narrow this range.",
