      "narrative": "Ursa Major Technologies is a Series E frontier-tech company in the Space & Aerospace sector, having raised $85M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-stage peers, including ICEYE, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries at similar or adjacent funding stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $85M total raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical for Series E advancement, implies a valuation of $119M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range spanning $1.6B (Varda Space Industries, Series D) to $12.0B (ICEYE, Series F). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue data for the target.\n\nTriangulation across these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $101M to $2.6B, with a median of $1.2B. The wide spread reflects meaningful dispersion within the peer set and methodological divergence. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor estimate, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher values. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, unit economics, and whether Ursa Major's competitive positioning aligns more closely with early-stage peers or later-stage operators like ICEYE. Additional clarity on current-stage fundraising terms and recent peer transactions would narrow this range materially.",
