      "narrative": "Mariana Minerals is a Series A\u2013stage climate and energy company founded by Turner Caldwell that has raised $95M+ to date. The valuation exercise draws on a Climate & Energy sector comp universe of nine private peers (including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen) and one public comparable (LNZA). A narrow-filter peer median approach proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within acceptable valuation tiers; only the stage-progression method yielded a quantitative datapoint.\n\nThe stage-progression method uses the $95M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage step-ups, implying a valuation of $190M. This single-method result limits confidence in triangulation but provides a central anchor. Using this as a median point with standard variance assumptions yields a low estimate of $162M and a high of $218M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M\u2013$218M with a median of $190M, though the single-method foundation introduces material uncertainty. Meaningful validation would require either identifying additional same-stage or near-stage Climate & Energy peers with disclosed valuations, or conducting a bottom-up revenue multiple or DCF sensitivity analysis tied to company-specific unit economics and market timing assumptions\u2014none of which are present in current data.",
