      "narrative": "d-Matrix is a Series C semiconductor chip company founded by Sid Sheth and Sudeep Bhoja, currently valued at $2.0B post-money following $450M in total capital raised. The valuation assessment triangulates across a comp universe of 8 private and 3 public semiconductor firms, including peers Etched ($5.0B, Series C), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C).\n\nTwo quantitative methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x multiplier to the $2.0B last post-money valuation, implying $3.4B. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $1.9B median (range: $529M\u2013$5.0B). Public-comp anchoring using P/S multiples from ALAB, NVDA, and AMD (sector median 21.5x) could not be applied due to absence of target revenue data, typical for private companies.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a range of $1.6B\u2013$3.9B, with a median of $2.6B. The current $2.0B valuation sits at the lower end of this range, reflecting early-stage risk and limited comparable transactions. Key uncertainties include the target's actual revenue run-rate, TAM penetration trajectory, and relative competitive position within a crowded chip-design space. Stage-progression and peer comparables diverge by $1.5B, underscoring valuation sensitivity to stage-specific capital efficiency assumptions and peer selection.",
