      "narrative": "Lumina Vehicles is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Ahmed Shubber (CEO) and Federico Di Palma, having raised $8M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company in the Robotics & Manufacturing sector, including peers such as Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $8M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage advancement, yielding $16M. Peer-median analysis samples four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging $1.1B to $2.0B. The median of this peer set is $1.7B, reflecting the strong valuations commanded by later-stage robotics companies in the current market.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $14M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $858M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the stage-progression method implies substantially lower value consistent with Lumina's Series A status and capital raised, while the peer-median approach assumes convergence toward later-stage comparable multiples. Key uncertainties include the degree to which Lumina's current operational metrics and market traction justify peer-level valuations, and the applicability of Series B+ comps to a Series A business.",
