      "narrative": "Fortastra is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $8M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates two applicable methods against a comp universe of 4 private peers at same or adjacent stage (Sierra Space at $8.0B Series C; Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B; Aalyria at $1.3B Series B; Skyryse at $1.1B Series C), supplemented by 5 public space and aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median 27.4x price-to-sales.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method, applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier to the $75M total-raised proxy, implies $142M. The Peer-Median method anchors to the $1.65B median across the 4 private comps, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples is not applicable due to lack of disclosed target revenue. These two methods triangulate to a median of $896M, with a low bound of $121M and a high bound of $1.9B.\n\nThe wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median reflects material uncertainty around whether Fortastra's technology maturity and market position align with the lower quartile of the peer set or mid-pack valuations. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, competitive differentiation relative to better-capitalized peers, and customer concentration. The peer-median of $1.65B should be weighted more heavily given sample size and stage alignment, though the $142M floor remains relevant if execution or market conditions deteriorate materially.",
