      "narrative": "Exotec, a Series D robotics and manufacturing company, has raised over $335M and carries a current post-money valuation of $2.0B. The valuation analysis incorporates a comparison universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable across the robotics and manufacturing sector, including peers such as Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), Agile Robots ($1.0B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, anchored to the $2.0B last post-money and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, yields $3.0B. Peer-median valuation across the four-company comparable set in the same sector and stage cohort produces $1.3B, with the peer range spanning $1.0B to $2.3B. The divergence between these methods reflects both the heterogeneity of the peer set across Series C and E stages and uncertainty in stage-specific multiple assumptions.\n\nTriangulation of the two methods supports a valuation range of $1.1B to $3.4B, with a median of $2.1B. The current $2.0B valuation sits near the lower bound of this range. Key sensitivities include the applicability of the 1.5x stage multiplier and whether later-stage peers (Divergent at Series E) or earlier-stage peers (Series C cohort) provide the most relevant pricing benchmark for a Series D company.",
