      "narrative": "Neko Health is a Series C-stage biotech company that has raised $326M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable universe of 3 public biotech peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage companies in the Biotech & Health sector, with particular focus on 3 same-stage private comparables: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy foundation ($700M) and applying a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $1.2B. Peer-median benchmarking across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range from $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via revenue multiples cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue figures for the target. \n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.0B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median point of $2.5B. Material uncertainty remains around the wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014a 3.3x spread between the median and the highest peer\u2014and the absence of revenue or profitability metrics for the target, which limits ability to differentiate Neko Health within its peer set.",
