      "narrative": "ispace is a public-stage space and aerospace company founded by Takeshi Hakamada that has raised $200M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage peers: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across these 4 public space and aerospace comparables is $5.2B, with a range spanning $840M at the low end (Astroscale) to $40.0B at the high end (Rocket Lab). A public-comp anchoring approach using price-to-sales multiples\u2014the sector median is 27.4x across 6 public tickers\u2014cannot be applied without disclosure of ispace's revenue, which is not on file.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.4B to $6.0B, centered on the peer median of $5.2B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion within the comp set ($840M to $40.0B) reflecting material differences in business maturity and market positioning, and the absence of revenue data to apply multiple-based methods. A single method drives this estimate, limiting triangulation robustness. Resolution of ispace's near-term revenue trajectory and competitive positioning relative to the Rocket Lab / Planet Labs tier would narrow this band materially.",
