      "narrative": "Rapidus is a late-stage semiconductor company that has raised $5.0B+ to date. The valuation landscape for frontier chip firms includes 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers such as Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems, though direct same-stage comparability remains limited.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the primary applicable valuation approach. Using total capital raised ($5.0B) as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical for late-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $6.0B. Public semiconductor comps trade at a median P/S multiple of 21.5x across the three tickers identified, but this cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures\u2014a standard limitation for private company analysis.\n\nThe triangulated range is $5.1B to $6.9B, with a midpoint of $6.0B supported by stage-progression logic alone. Key uncertainties include the absence of narrow-set peer valuations in the semiconductor frontier-tech segment, lack of revenue disclosure enabling multiple-based approaches, and limited visibility into capital efficiency relative to disclosed private competitors. The single-method derivation suggests material sensitivity to stage-progression assumptions and argues for direct revenue benchmarking or transaction data once available.",
