      "narrative": "Innospace is a public-stage space and aerospace company founded by Kim Soo-Jong that has raised $80M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage peers: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach given available data. The median valuation across these four public space and aerospace companies is $5.2B, with a wide range spanning $840M at the low end to $40.0B at the high end. A public-comp multiples approach using the sector's median P/S of 27.4x across 6 public tickers cannot be applied due to the absence of Innospace's revenue on file. Revenue disclosure remains uncommon for private companies and limits the applicability of earnings or revenue-based methodologies.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $4.4B to $6.0B, anchored at the peer median of $5.2B. The wide dispersion in comparable valuations\u2014from Astroscale's $840M to Rocket Lab's $40.0B\u2014reflects material uncertainty in how the market prices space-sector operators at comparable development stages. Stage of operational maturity, launch cadence, and customer concentration drive significant variance within this peer set. Without audited financials or revenue guidance from Innospace, the median-based estimate carries inherent modeling risk.",
