      "narrative": "Skyroot Aerospace is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $160M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of six same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies spanning Series B through Series D, including Sierra Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, and Aalyria, alongside five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $160M fundraising proxy, implying a $272M valuation. Peer-median benchmarking across the six same-sector comparable companies yields a $1.8B implied valuation, with the peer set ranging from $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied given the absence of disclosed revenue data. The public sector median trades at 27.4x price-to-sales, but this multiple cannot be calibrated to Skyroot without revenue visibility.\n\nTriangulating these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $231M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.0B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around commercialization trajectory and market capture relative to more mature peers like Sierra Space. Stage-progression conservatively anchors the floor; peer multiples capture sector-level risk and growth expectations. Revenue disclosure or near-term funding events would materially narrow this range.",
