      "narrative": "Tenstorrent, a Series D semiconductor design company founded by Milos Trajkovic, is valued at $2.7B post-money following $1B+ in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public semiconductor names (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including Etched, d-Matrix, DEEPX, Cerebras, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nTwo methods triangulate forward value. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.5x step-up multiplier from Series D to the next funding round, implying $4.0B. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps (Etched at $5.0B, d-Matrix at $2.0B, DEEPX at $529M) yields a median of $2.0B, with a range of $529M to $5.0B. Public-comp anchoring using a 21.5x P/S multiple across the three public peers cannot be applied\u2014Tenstorrent's revenue is not on file, a common constraint for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.7B (low) to $4.7B (high), with a median of $3.0B. This range reflects material dispersion in peer valuations and stage-progression assumptions. Key uncertainties include the timing and structure of the next funding event, revenue trajectory relative to comparable-stage private peers, and the durability of current public semiconductor multiples.",
