      "narrative": "SunDrive Solar is a Seed-stage solar technology company in the Climate & Energy sector, founded by Vince Allen and David Hu. The sector comprises 9 private peers (including later-stage ventures like Helion, Redwood Materials, and QuantumScape) and 1 public comparable (Lonza Group, ticker LNZA), though no proximate same-stage or adjacent-stage peers exist with sufficient data density for median-based triangulation.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable methodology here. Using total capital raised ($60M+ including the November 2025 A$25.3M ARENA grant) as a proxy baseline of $4M in nominal founding capital, a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the next institutional round implies a valuation of $10M. This method captures the expected dilution and funding velocity characteristic of climate-tech ventures at this stage.\n\nThe Peer-Median method is not applicable; while the Climate & Energy sector contains nine comparable companies, none qualify as narrow-filter peers at the same or adjacent stage with similar valuation tiers. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material bias.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $8M to $12M, with a median point of $10M. Key uncertainties include the timing and structure of the next institutional funding round, the deployment rate of the ARENA grant capital, and whether SunDrive's perovskite-tandem technology achieves the efficiency milestones necessary to justify venture-scale returns. The single-method triangulation also limits confidence; further data on comparable Seed-stage climate hardware exits would narrow this band.",
