      "narrative": "Monumental is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Salar al Khafaji and Sebastiaan Visser that has raised $32M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public equity in the sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $32M total raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a $61M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B), yielding a median valuation of $1.8B with a range of $1.6B\u2013$2.0B.\n\nThe wide spread between methods ($61M to $1.8B median to $2.0B high) reflects material uncertainty in how to anchor Monumental's value within the frontier robotics market. The stage-progression method likely underweights the sector's current funding intensity and valuations. The peer-median approach assumes sufficient operational comparability; however, the selection of only three comps and their own stage-specific heterogeneity introduce discretion risk. A defensible range is $52M\u2013$2.0B, with the $905M median point representing an equally-weighted midpoint. Resolution hinges on Monumental's specific technology differentiation, customer traction, and pathway to defending its position within a cohort of heavily capitalized competitors.",
