      "narrative": "RobCo is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Roman H\u00f6lzl, Paul Maroldt, and Constantin Dresel, having raised $160M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private peers (Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics among others) and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-Progression applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement to a $1.4B total-raised proxy, implying $2.7B. Peer-Median derives valuation from four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Generalist AI at Series B ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics at Series B ($1.8B), Dexterity at Series B ($1.6B), and Walden Robotics at Seed ($1.1B). The median across this set is $1.7B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $1.4B (low) to $3.1B (high), with a median of $2.2B. The $800M spread between methods reflects two key uncertainties: (1) whether RobCo's capital deployment aligns with peers' post-Series A trajectories, and (2) the relative weighting of Stage-Progression versus peer-market comps in a frontier sector where comparable transaction frequency remains limited.",
