      "narrative": "Deep Isolation, a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Elizabeth Muller and Richard A. Muller, has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 private and 3 public companies in the nuclear energy sector, including peers at adjacent stages: Fuse Energy (Series A, $200M), Nano Nuclear Energy (Seed, $808M), and Valar Atomics (Series B, $6.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement to the $26M total raised proxy, implying a $52M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps yields a median valuation of $808M, with a range spanning $200M to $6.0B. The wide peer range reflects heterogeneous company maturity and technology focus within the nuclear energy space.\n\nSynthesizing both methods yields a triangulated range of $44M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $430M. The significant spread between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects material uncertainty around Deep Isolation's relative competitive position within its peer set. Key drivers of valuation uncertainty include the company's current technical progress relative to the broader cohort, capital efficiency trajectory, and sector-level funding momentum in advanced nuclear technologies. Stage-progression alone likely underweights recent market enthusiasm for the sector; peer-median results should be weighted accordingly pending visibility into Deep Isolation's proprietary differentiation and near-term milestones.",
