      "narrative": "Locus Robotics, a Series F robotics and manufacturing company, is valued at $2.0B post-money and has raised $438M to date. The valuation is anchored against a peer universe of 9 same-sector companies in similar valuation tiers, comprising 1 public company and 8 private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applied a typical 1.3x multiplier to the $2.0B last post-money valuation, implying $2.6B for the next stage. Peer-median analysis across the 9-company cohort yielded a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.3B. This wider dispersion reflects heterogeneity in stage and timing across the peer set.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.4B to $3.0B, with a median of $2.1B. The current $2.0B valuation sits near the lower bound of this range, suggesting modest upside to the median case. Key uncertainties include the timing and terms of the next financing round, which will materially impact stage-progression methodology, and the quality-adjusted performance differential between Locus and its peer cohort, particularly given the dispersion in peer valuations. The peer-median method carries limited precision given stage diversity within the comparison set.",
