      "narrative": "Kepler Communications is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $200M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 6 private peers at similar or adjacent funding stages, alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable here. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $200M total raised proxy, yielding $340M. Peer-median anchoring across 6 same-sector comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B), Apex Space ($2.3B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and one additional peer\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp pricing via price-to-sales cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure. The peer range reflects material heterogeneity in funding stage and business model maturity within the cohort.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $289M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.1B across the two applicable methods. Stage-progression yields the lower bound; peer-median drives the midpoint. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, capital intensity, path to unit economics, and the wide dispersion among private comparables\u2014particularly the outsized $8.0B Sierra Space valuation, which significantly widens confidence intervals.",
