      "narrative": "Reaction Dynamics is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Bachar Elzein that has raised C$38M to date. The valuation exercise drew from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, representing 13 total reference points in the Space & Aerospace sector.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only stage-progression proved applicable. The peer-median approach was not viable; while 14 same-sector peers exist, fewer than three datapoints clustered at comparable stage and valuation tier. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, a standard constraint for private company analysis. The stage-progression method applied a 2.0x multiplier to the C$38M capital raised proxy, yielding an implied Series A valuation of C$76M.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range of C$65M (low) to C$87M (high), centered at C$76M median, reflects the singular applicable method and its inherent step-up assumption. Key uncertainties include: reliance on a single methodology rather than cross-validation; lack of revenue or unit-economics visibility to calibrate against public multiples; and the absence of sufficient same-stage private comparables to anchor expectations within Reaction Dynamics' specific niche. A fuller assessment would require disclosure of financial performance or operational metrics to enable public-comp or precedent transaction anchoring.",
