      "narrative": "LabGenius, a seed-stage biotech company founded by James Field, has raised $73M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies in the Biotech & Health sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the sole applicable approach. Using total capital raised ($73M) as a proxy for enterprise value at seed stage, a normalized base value of $27M is adjusted by a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $68M. Peer-median comparison cannot be performed; while 7 same-sector peers exist, none met the threshold of \u22653 datapoints within narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier). Public-comp anchoring using the Biotech & Health sector P/S median of 6.6x is inapplicable due to absence of target revenue disclosure, standard for private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $57M to $78M, with a median point of $68M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around stage-progression output. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the $27M base-value proxy relative to actual deployment and burn, the stability of 2.5x as a step-up multiplier for this company's profile, and the absence of revenue-based market validation. Additional founder or investor data would strengthen conviction.",
