      "narrative": "Mission Barns is a Series B biotech company founded by Eitan Fischer and David Bowman that has raised $50M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in Biotech & Health, including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), New Limit ($3.1B, Series C), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M, Series B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression approach applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $50M total raised proxy, implying a $95M valuation. The peer-median method uses four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $3.5B (range: $539M\u2013$10.3B). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. The wide peer range reflects heterogeneity in biotech maturity and technology stage.\n\nThe two-method triangulation produces a median estimate of $1.8B, with a low of $81M and a high of $4.0B. The substantial dispersion between stage-progression ($95M) and peer-median ($3.5B) reflects material uncertainty around whether Mission Barns' economics and technology trajectory align with higher-valued peers or more nascent biotech entrants. Key uncertainties include target revenue, clinical/commercial progress relative to peers, and whether peer comparables adequately reflect sector-specific risk.",
