      "narrative": "Cresilon, a Series B biotech and health company founded by Joe Landolina, has raised $113M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 8 private peers and 3 public companies in biotech and health, including late-stage companies like Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B), alongside earlier-stage comparables like Eikon Therapeutics ($539M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $113M capital raised, implying a $215M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $3.5B median valuation, with a range of $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as Cresilon's revenue is not disclosed. These two methods produce a triangulated range of $182M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B.\n\nThe wide dispersion\u2014spanning nearly a 22x range\u2014reflects substantial uncertainty in stage-appropriate valuation. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively at $215M; the peer median at $3.5B suggests meaningfully higher value if Cresilon's pipeline and clinical progress track toward the upper tier of comparables. Key uncertainties include pipeline advancement, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether recent fundraising or clinical milestones position the company toward Series C valuations observed in the peer set.",
