      "narrative": "Sage Geosystems is a Series B climate and energy technology company that has raised $114M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Linzatech, LNZA) operating in the same sector, including adjacent-stage companies such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($114M) as a proxy valuation floor and applies a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implying $217M. The peer-median approach identifies three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), producing a median valuation of $1.0B and a range of $700M\u2013$3.0B. This peer set reflects meaningful heterogeneity in later-stage funding outcomes within climate tech.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $184M to $1.1B, with a median point estimate of $608M. The wide range reflects two primary uncertainties: the compression between stage-progression (implying $217M) and peer multiples (implying $1.0B median), and the dispersion within the peer set itself. Stage and capital efficiency relative to comparable companies remain key valuation drivers.",
