      "narrative": "Asimov is a Series B biotech company that has raised $209M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 8 private companies and 3 public comparables in Biotech & Health, anchored by four same-sector peers at Series B\u2013C stage: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), New Limit ($3.1B), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression methodology, using total raised ($209M) as a proxy and applying a typical 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $397M. Peer-median methodology across the four comparable companies yields a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Asimov's revenue is not disclosed. Public biotech median P/S is 6.6x across 3 tickers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L), but lacks applicability without target revenue data.\n\nThe triangulated range is $338M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B across the two applicable methods. The wide spread reflects meaningful uncertainty: stage-progression yields a conservative floor, while peer-median is heavily influenced by outlier valuations at Colossal ($10.3B). Key uncertainties include the target's current clinical-stage maturity, intellectual property scope relative to peers, and runway relative to next funding event. Revenue disclosure would enable public-comp triangulation and narrow the band materially.",
