      "narrative": "Cemvita is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Moji and Tara Karimi that has raised $30M to date. The valuation landscape includes one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers spanning similar and adjacent stages, with KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Amogy, Helion, and Redwood Materials representing the most relevant reference set.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $30M total raised as a proxy for enterprise value, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage progression, implying $57M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies\u2014KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C)\u2014yields a median of $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B. The stage-progression method reflects earlier-stage methodology while peer comparables capture recent market pricing for similar-risk climate-tech ventures.\n\nTriangulating these approaches yields a valuation range of $48M (conservative stage-progression floor) to $1.1B (high peer comparable), with a median of $528M. The substantial spread reflects material uncertainty around Cemvita's technology maturity, path to revenue, and capital efficiency relative to the peer set. Stage and underlying technology differentiation are critical variables not fully captured by these methods alone.",
