      "narrative": "Infleqtion, a publicly traded quantum computing company founded by Dana Anderson, carries a current market valuation of $1.92B following $760M+ in cumulative capital raised. The peer universe for this stage and sector consists of four directly comparable public-stage quantum computing firms: IonQ ($13.0B), D-Wave Quantum ($6.3B), Rigetti Computing ($4.5B), and Archer Materials ($60M).\n\nThe peer-median method, the applicable triangulation approach given available data, yields a median valuation of $5.4B across this four-company cohort. The peer range spans from $60M to $13.0B, reflecting substantial dispersion in market assessment of quantum computing value creation at this maturity level. This median of $5.4B implies a valuation range of $4.6B to $6.2B when bracketed at 15% confidence intervals.\n\nInfleqtion's current $1.92B valuation sits materially below the peer median, suggesting either a market discount relative to comparable-stage operators or differentiated risk pricing. The wide peer distribution\u2014a 216x spread between lowest and highest valuations\u2014underscores the high uncertainty endemic to quantum computing asset pricing at the public stage. Key uncertainties include quantum computing's path to commercialization, heterogeneity in technical approaches across the peer set, and whether current public valuations reflect speculative or grounded near-term revenue expectations. A single-method analysis limits confidence; additional comparable transaction or revenue-multiple data would strengthen conviction in any narrowed range.",
