      "narrative": "DEEPX is a Series C-stage semiconductor company founded by Lokwon Kim, currently valued at $529M post-money following $103M in total capital raised. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 8 private and 3 public firms in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including peers such as Etched, Tenstorrent, d-Matrix, and Positron AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $899M. Peer-median analysis across 4 same-sector and same/adjacent-stage companies yields a median valuation of $2.4B, with a range spanning $1.0B (Positron AI, Series B) to $5.0B (Etched, Series C). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied due to DEEPX's undisclosed revenue. The three public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) trade at a median P/S of 21.5x, but this method requires target revenue data.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $764M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.6B across the two applicable methods. The wide range reflects material uncertainty around DEEPX's revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to its peer set, which spans a five-fold valuation spread. Current post-money sits below the triangulated range, suggesting either a valuation gap or material risk factors not captured in stage-based comparables.",
