      "narrative": "Nascent Materials is a seed-stage company in the Climate & Energy sector founded by Chaitanya Sharma, having raised $2.3M to date. The broader sector comprises one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen, though none qualify as tight stage-matched comparables.\n\nThe valuation analysis relies on a single applicable method: stage-progression analysis. Using the $2.3M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, this method implies a valuation of $5.75M. The peer-median approach was deemed inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage datapoints within the Climate & Energy sector\u2014while nine peers operate in the sector, none met the minimum threshold of three comparable companies at similar stage and valuation tier.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $5M to $7M, with a median of $6M, derived from the single stage-progression method. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer benchmarking, which limits confidence in the step-up multiplier selected, and the lack of granular financial metrics (revenue, burn rate, or IP defensibility indicators) for the target company. Any final valuation should incorporate operational performance data and more detailed comparable transaction analysis as additional data becomes available.",
