      "narrative": "Marathon Fusion is a seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Adam Rutkowski and Kyle Schiller. The company has raised $10.9M to date. The nuclear energy sector comprises 11 comparable companies: three public entities (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and eight private firms including Nano Nuclear Energy, Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nA single valuation method proved applicable to this analysis. The stage-progression approach uses the $10.9M total raised as a base proxy value and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement in the sector. This yields an implied valuation of $27M. A peer-median approach was not viable; while five nuclear energy comparables exist, the narrow peer filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar valuation tier) did not return sufficient datapoints (minimum three required), and a broad cross-sector median would introduce undue noise.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $23M (low) to $31M (high), with a median of $27M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method and should be interpreted with appropriate caution. Key uncertainties include the appropriate stage-progression multiplier for nuclear energy specifically, the absence of directly comparable seed-stage nuclear peers, and limited visibility into Marathon Fusion's technical progress or capital efficiency relative to the broader comp set. Additional fundraising or operational milestones would improve conviction in final valuation placement within this range.",
