      "narrative": "Remedy Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by David Bell and Jake Sganga that has raised $35M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014including Series B stage firms Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B), as well as Seed-stage Walden Robotics ($1.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $35M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage advancement, yielding $70M. The peer-median method anchors to four robotics/manufacturing peers at same or adjacent stage, producing a median valuation of $1.7B with a range from $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $60M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $885M. The wide range reflects substantial dispersion between stage-progression and peer comparables, indicating material uncertainty in how much of the peer set's later-stage valuations apply to Remedy at Series A. Key dependencies include whether capital deployment trajectory and operational milestones align with the Series B cohort versus earlier-stage peers, and whether robotics sector multiples remain sustained.",
