      "narrative": "Elementary Robotics is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $66M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 private-market comparables in the same sector and stage (Hadrian at $1.6B, Agile Robots at $1.0B, and Nimble Robotics at $1.0B), supplemented by a broader set of 8 private peers and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total capital raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C-to-Series D progression, yielding $112M. The peer-median method references the $1.0B median valuation across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables, with a documented range of $1.0B to $1.6B. These methods produce divergent outputs, reflecting the wide dispersion between bootstrap-adjusted models and peer multiples in frontier robotics.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $95M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median estimate of $556M. The 12x spread between low and high reflects material uncertainty around which comparables are most relevant\u2014whether Elementary Robotics' profile aligns with the capital-efficient base (stage-progression) or the higher-valued peers (peer-median). Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to named peers, revenue traction, and capital efficiency relative to the peer set. Additional data on revenue, burn rate, and product-market fit would narrow this range materially.",
