      "narrative": "Akash Systems, a Series B frontier-tech company in Space & Aerospace founded by Felix Ejeckam and Ty Mitchell, has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms, with peer valuations ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B.\n\nTwo methods triangulate to a defensible range. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $40M raised proxy, implying $76M. Peer-median anchoring uses four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B Series C)\u2014yielding a median of $1.6B and a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring was not applied; the Space & Aerospace sector median multiple is 27.4x across six tickers, but Akash's revenue is not disclosed, precluding a revenue-based valuation.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a range of $65M to $1.9B, with a median of $863M. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty: stage-progression conservatively suggests ~$76M, while peer medians imply substantially higher valuation. Key variables include Akash's revenue trajectory, competitive positioning relative to Series B peers like Cowboy Space, and stage-specific capital efficiency. Revenue disclosure and tighter peer revenue comparability would narrow this range materially.",
