      "narrative": "Mythic is a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $125M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 8 private semiconductor peers at similar or adjacent stages\u2014including Tenstorrent (Series D, $2.7B), d-Matrix (Series C, $2.0B), Etched (Series C, $5.0B), and DEEPX (Series C, $529M)\u2014alongside 3 public semiconductor comparables (NVDA, AMD, ALAB).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $125M total raised, implying $188M valuation. Peer-Median analysis across the 4-company sample yields a median valuation of $2.4B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. Public-Comp Anchoring via P/S multiples (21.5x median across the public set) cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure. These two methods triangulate to a low of $159M, a median of $1.3B, and a high of $2.7B.\n\nThe wide $159M\u2013$2.7B range reflects meaningful uncertainty around Mythic's competitive positioning and commercialization progress within a crowded frontier-chip segment. The peer median of $2.4B sits above the triangulated median, driven by outlier valuations at Etched and Tenstorrent. Stage-Progression suggests more conservative valuation grounded in capital deployed; Peer-Median reflects market sentiment for late-stage semiconductor hardware ventures. Key uncertainties include product-market validation, customer concentration, and differentiation relative to well-funded incumbents in the comp set.",
