      "narrative": "Xsight Labs is a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $281M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Etched, Tenstorrent, d-Matrix, DEEPX) valued between $529M and $5.0B, anchored by a median of $2.4B. Public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) exist but cannot be applied without target revenue disclosure.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for Series D valuation and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for the next funding round, implies $422M. Peer-median analysis directly references the $2.4B median across the four same-sector peers, weighted toward Tenstorrent's $2.7B Series D valuation as the most relevant comparable. These methods diverge materially, reflecting uncertainty about Xsight's market position relative to peers.\n\nThe triangulated range is $358M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.4B across the two methods. The low end reflects stage-based progression; the high end anchors to peer median. Key uncertainties include the target's revenue scale and competitive differentiation within the crowded frontier-chip segment, where peer valuations span a 9.5x range. Revenue visibility and pathway to profitability would materially tighten this band.",
