      "narrative": "Electra is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Sandeep Nijhawan and Quoc Pham that has raised $299M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 companies (1 public, 8 private) in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages, including KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Amogy, Helion, and Redwood Materials.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $299M in total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 1.9x multiplier for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $568M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $483M to $1.1B, with a median of $784M. Key uncertainties include the dispersion among peer valuations (driven by differences in technology maturity and funding round timing) and the limited precision of total raised as a valuation proxy for an unpriced Series B. The peer-median result skews materially higher than stage-progression, suggesting market appetite for climate-energy infrastructure may be outpacing typical round-step multiples, though this gap warrants validation against round-by-round pricing history if available.",
