      "narrative": "Biobot Analytics, a Series B biotech company founded by Mariana Matus and Newsha Ghaeli, has raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 11 comparable companies: 3 public-market biotech firms (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Eikon Therapeutics, Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $40M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $76M. The peer-median method anchors to four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $3.5B, though the range is wide ($539M to $10.3B), reflecting substantial dispersion across the cohort. Public-market anchoring using a biotech sector P/S multiple of 6.6x cannot be applied owing to the absence of disclosed revenue data for the target.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods yields a valuation range of $65M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B. The wide band reflects material tension between the stage-progression result and peer multiples, suggesting either that peer valuations embed meaningful premium for scale or proof-of-concept not yet demonstrated by Biobot, or that peer multiples are unsustainably elevated. Stage of capital deployment, competitive positioning within the diagnostic biotech subsector, and revenue trajectory constitute the primary variables that would narrow this range.",
