      "narrative": "Amber Bio is a seed-stage biotech company founded by Basem Al-Shayeb and Jacob Borrajo that has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public peers in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private firms including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised as a proxy for seed-stage value ($26M) and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier for progression to the next funding stage yields an implied valuation of $65M. Peer-median analysis was not executable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the Biotech & Health sector\u2014fewer than three datapoints met narrow filtering criteria. Public-comp anchoring using the sector's 6.6x P/S multiple (median across three public tickers) could not be applied because Amber Bio's revenue is not disclosed, which is typical for early-stage private biotech.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $55M to $75M, with $65M as the central point. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 2.5x multiplier for Amber Bio's specific technical and commercial profile, the absence of revenue visibility, and limited precision from a single applicable method. Investors should seek additional market intelligence on recent biotech seed-to-Series A rounds and Amber Bio's specific IP and development status to narrow this band.",
