      "narrative": "Manifold Bio is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Gleb Kuznetsov and Pierce Ogden, having raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, including companies such as Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using the $40M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for progression from Series A to subsequent funding rounds, this method implies a valuation of $80M. Peer-Median analysis was not feasible due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum sample criteria (fewer than 3 datapoints after filtering). Public-Comp Anchoring could not be executed because Manifold Bio's revenue is not disclosed, precluding application of the 6.6x median P/S multiple observed across the three public peers.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $68M to $92M, with a median of $80M. This range reflects modest downside and upside around the stage-progression result, accounting for uncertainty inherent in a single-method analysis. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data to validate public multiples and limited narrow-peer disclosure, which constrains cross-check validation. The valuation is most sensitive to execution risk and capital efficiency relative to comparable Series A programs in the sector.",
