      "narrative": "Signaloid is a seed-stage semiconductor company that has raised $10M to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector contains 11 comparable companies across public and private markets, including public anchors ALAB, NVDA, and AMD, and private peers such as Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched. However, the private comparable set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage depth to support a reliable peer-median valuation.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable triangulation method here. Using total capital raised as a proxy for seed-stage valuation ($10M) and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the next funding round yields an implied valuation of $25M. Public semiconductor comps trade at a median 21.5x price-to-sales across the three anchor tickers, but this method cannot be applied without Signaloid's revenue figure, which is not disclosed. The narrow peer set in Chips & Semiconductors (zero same-stage, one adjacent-stage, and zero similar-tier comps meeting filtering criteria) precludes reliable peer-median anchoring.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $21M to $29M, centered at $25M. This range reflects stage-progression mechanics applied to disclosed capital raised. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable seed-stage semiconductor transactions, undisclosed revenue metrics that would enable public-comp triangulation, and the sector-specific risk profile of frontier chip development companies. The single-method foundation warrants cautious application of this range pending additional data disclosure or transaction activity.",
