      "narrative": "Apis Cor is a seed-stage construction technology company that has raised $5.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a private comparable universe of five companies operating in housing and construction technology, including BotBuilt, Unlimited Industries, Ground Control Development, ADMARES, and Hedral. No public market comps are available in this nascent sector.\n\nThe stage-progression method was applied as the primary valuation approach. Using total capital raised ($5.5M, rounded to $6M) as a proxy for seed-stage value, a 2.5x multiplier\u2014typical for progression from seed to Series A\u2014yields an implied valuation of $14M. This multiplier reflects the risk reduction and validation expected between stages in early-stage venture investing.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $12M to $16M, with a median point estimate of $14M. The relatively narrow band reflects limited methodological diversity given available data; triangulation relies on a single method applied with conservative, mid-case, and optimistic assumptions. Key uncertainties include the company's pre-revenue or early-revenue status, the absence of public benchmarks in construction tech, and reliance on stage-based multipliers rather than comparable company multiples. Validation through additional precedent transaction data or revenue-based metrics would strengthen conviction in any specific valuation within this range.",
