      "narrative": "Starfish Space is a Series B\u2013stage space and aerospace company that has raised $100M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse) alongside five public Space & Aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), which trade at a median price-to-sales multiple of 27.4x.\n\nTwo quantitative methods apply to this target. Stage-progression analysis, using $100M in total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $190M. Peer-median anchoring across the four private comparables produces $1.6B; these peers range from $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space), with an interquartile concentration around $1.3B\u2013$2.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied: the sector median P/S of 27.4x is observable, but Starfish Space's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a range of $162M to $1.9B, with a median of $920M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: the peer-median method assumes Starfish Space's competitive positioning and go-to-market trajectory match those of larger, later-stage cohort peers, while stage-progression alone underweights market-based peer evidence. Revenue visibility and path to profitability remain critical unknowns informing placement within the range.",
