      "narrative": "TS Conductor is a Series B climate and energy company that has raised $60M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparator (Lnza), spanning advanced materials, energy storage, and industrial decarbonization across similar and adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($60M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $114M. Peer-median analysis employs three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C). The median across this set is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $97M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $557M. The wide spread between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects genuine uncertainty inherent in early-stage climate tech. Stage-progression conservatively anchors to realized capital and near-term progression patterns, while peer-median captures the outsized valuations typical of well-funded frontier energy plays. Key uncertainties include unit economics clarity, technology risk mitigation, and the timing and path to revenue scale\u2014factors that typically explain valuation dispersion within the peer set.",
