      "narrative": "Mytra, a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Chris Walti and Ahmad Baitalmal, has raised over $200M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies (1 public, 8 private) including Hadrian, Agile Robots, and Nimble Robotics at the same stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses the $200M raised as a proxy for current enterprise value and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C to later-stage step-ups, yielding $340M. The peer-median method examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $1.0B to $1.6B (Hadrian at the high end), producing a median implied value of $1.0B. These approaches reflect fundamentally different assumptions about Mytra's competitive positioning relative to named peers.\n\nTriangulating both methods across low, median, and high scenarios produces a range of $289M to $1.1B, with a midpoint of $670M. The 1.7x dispersion between methods reflects material uncertainty around whether Mytra's traction and market position align closer to Stage C base dynamics or to the upper quartile of peer valuations. Key uncertainties include revenue run rate, gross margin profile, customer concentration, and manufacturing scale relative to the three peers used in the median calculation.",
