      "narrative": "HyImpulse is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac74 million to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse at adjacent stages.\n\nTwo methodologies prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the \u20ac74 million total raised and applying a typical 1.9x multiplier for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $141 million. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $1.6 billion median valuation, with a range of $1.1 billion to $8.0 billion. The wide peer range reflects material dispersion in the market: Skyryse and Aalyria trade near $1.1\u2013$1.3 billion at Series B/C, while Sierra Space reaches $8.0 billion at Series C. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. \n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $120 million to $1.9 billion, with a median of $895 million. The wide band reflects fundamental tension between stage-progression methodology, which conservatively scales capital deployed, and peer comparables, which capture market pricing at adjacent stages. Key uncertainties include the degree to which HyImpulse's market position and capital efficiency align with the peer cohort, and whether comparable companies' valuations reflect durable fundamentals or sector cyclicality.",
