      "narrative": "SpliceBio is a Series B biotech company founded by Miquel Vila-Perell\u00ad\u00f3 that has raised $135M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, and Eikon Therapeutics) spanning $539M to $10.3B, plus 3 public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression anchors to the $135M total raised and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying $256M. Peer-median valuation across the 4 same-sector/stage comps yields $3.5B, with a range from $539M (Eikon Therapeutics at Series B) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences at Series C). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because SpliceBio's revenue is not disclosed, which is standard for private companies. The public P/S median of 6.6x across the 3 tickers lacks a denominator to operate.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $218M to $4.0B, with a median of $1.9B across the two applicable methods. The wide spread reflects material stage and scale variation within the peer set\u2014particularly the outlier positioning of Colossal at $10.3B versus Eikon at $539M. Key uncertainties include SpliceBio's revenue trajectory relative to peers, clinical-stage risk profile, and whether comparable Series C valuations appropriately anchor a Series B target.",
