      "narrative": "Nu Quantum, a Series A quantum computing company founded by Carmen Palacios-Berraquero, is evaluated against a sector universe comprising 3 public comps (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing, and Infleqtion.\n\nThe stage-progression method is applicable and yields a $120M valuation. This approach uses the company's $60M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, implying a $120M post-money valuation. The peer-median approach is not applicable; while 6 same-sector peers exist, insufficient datapoints meet the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier clustering). Applying an all-sector median would risk material distortion given quantum computing's heterogeneous stage distribution and funding patterns.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $102M (low) to $138M (median to high), centered at $120M. Key uncertainties include the scarcity of directly comparable Series A quantum hardware entrants and the stage-progression multiplier's sensitivity to market conditions and capital availability in deep-tech infrastructure. Refinement of this range would require either additional quantum-specific Series A or late Seed comparables, or forward-looking revenue or technical milestone data not available in the current dataset.",
