      "narrative": "Pragmatic Semiconductor is a Series D frontier-semiconductor company founded by Richard Price and Scott White that has raised $231M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two applicable methodologies within a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Etched, Tenstorrent, d-Matrix, DEEPX) alongside 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nThe Stage-Progression method, applying a 1.5x multiplier typical for Series D advancement to the $231M capital raised proxy, implies a valuation of $346M. The Peer-Median approach across the 4 private comparables\u2014which range from $529M to $5.0B\u2014yields a median valuation of $2.4B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (21.5x median across the public set) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures, which private companies typically do not disclose.\n\nTriangulating these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $295M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage-specific discount rates and peer heterogeneity; notably, Tenstorrent at Series D achieved $2.7B while DEEPX at Series C valued at $529M. Key sensitivities include nearterm capital intensity, revenue trajectory, and competitive differentiation within the AI-silicon subsector. The peer-median approach currently dominates the analysis given available data constraints.",
