      "narrative": "Pulsar Fusion is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $15M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The Stage-Progression method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $15M raised proxy, yielding an implied valuation of $28M. The Peer-Median method references four same-sector peers at Series B/C stages: Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Aalyria ($1.3B), Skyryse ($1.1B), and Sierra Space ($8.0B). The median across these four peers is $1.6B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to unavailable revenue data for the target. \n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $24M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $839M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the Stage-Progression floor assumes minimal value creation beyond deployment of capital, while the Peer-Median approach captures heterogeneity in late-stage frontier-tech valuations. Key uncertainties include the target's revenue trajectory, technical validation milestones, and how comparably-funded peers' valuations reflect their respective de-risking progress.",
