      "narrative": "Hadean is a Series B-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities operating in the same sector and stage. Key private peers include Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $40M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $76M. Peer-median analysis across the 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a $1.0B implied valuation, with the peer set ranging from $300M to $3.0B. This wide dispersion reflects meaningful heterogeneity in market positioning and maturity within the Defense & Security frontier-tech category.\n\nThe triangulated range is $65M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $538M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects tension between Hadean's capital raised to date and the valuation multiples commanded by established Series B peers in this sector. Key uncertainties include customer concentration, technology differentiation relative to named peers, and near-term revenue trajectory. Further due diligence on traction metrics and competitive moat would narrow this range materially.",
