      "narrative": "Nordic Air Defence is a seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Karl Rosander. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 private companies and 2 public peers (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) operating in the same sector. The peer set includes both seed and Series A stage companies, with valuations ranging from $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe analysis applies a peer-median method across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Stark Defence ($4.0B, Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A). The median valuation across this cohort is $700M, with a range spanning from $125M to $4.0B. This method is the primary quantitative anchor given available data constraints.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $595M (low), $700M (median), and $805M (high). However, given that only one valuation method is fully applicable and the peer set spans two stages with significant valuation dispersion\u2014particularly the $4.0B outlier\u2014key uncertainties remain around Nordic Air Defence's relative technical maturity, customer traction, and capital efficiency versus the comparables. The wide range between low and high estimates reflects this methodological constraint. Additional data on revenue, headcount, or customer pipeline would refine confidence in this range.",
