      "narrative": "KrattWorks is a Series A\u2013stage Defense & Security company founded by Mattias Luha and T\u00f5nis Voitka. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers (2 public, 8 private), with core comparables including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo methods were applied to triangulate value. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's \u20ac19.7M ($20M equivalent) total raised as a baseline and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A progression to earlier-stage valuations, implying $39M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables (Stark Defence at $4.0B, Singularity at $400M, NODA AI at $125M) produces a median of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneity in funding trajectories and technology maturity within defense-tech.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a range of $33M to $460M, with a median of $220M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer-median anchors the upper half. Key uncertainties include customer concentration and contract stability in the defense sector, competitive positioning relative to the high-valuation outliers, and stage-appropriate burn dynamics. Without disclosed financials beyond revenue, profitability and path to Series B remain opaque.",
