      "narrative": "Cailabs is a Series C space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac57M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 6 private peers in the same sector and stage, including Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), and Varda Space Industries ($1.6B, Series D), alongside 5 public space and aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $57M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implies $97M. Peer-median analysis across 6 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Cailabs' revenue is not on file.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $82M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $943M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around stage progression timing and the substantial heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014particularly the $8.0B outlier (Sierra Space). The analysis is most robust within the $500M\u2013$1.2B band, where stage-adjusted fundamentals and median peer positioning converge. Revenue disclosure and a narrowed peer filter by sub-sector specificity would materially reduce range width.",
