      "narrative": "Ephos is a Seed-stage semiconductor design company founded by Andrea Rocchetto, Francesco Ceccarelli, and Ciro Pentangelo. The target operates within a frontier-tech subsector where 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and PsiQuantum provide market context.\n\nValuation analysis is constrained by data availability typical of early-stage semiconductor ventures. Stage-progression methodology proved applicable: using $42M in total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next-stage yields $104M. Peer-median valuation was not feasible\u2014while 12 same-sector private companies exist, none produced a sufficiently narrow comparable set (minimum 3 required at same or adjacent stage). Public-comp anchoring using the semiconductor sector's 21.5x median P/S multiple could not be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies at this maturity.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $88M to $119M, with $104M as the central estimate. This range reflects sensitivity around the stage-progression multiplier and acknowledges that meaningful peer triangulation remains unavailable. Key uncertainties include lack of disclosed revenue, absence of comparable seed-stage chip-design transactions, and the inherent volatility of early-stage semiconductor valuations. Any refinement requires either additional transaction data or direct revenue disclosure from the target.",
