      "narrative": "AAVantgarde Bio is a Series B biotech company founded by Alberto Auricchio and Natalia Misciattelli that has raised $141M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, and Eikon Therapeutics) valued between $539M and $10.3B, plus 3 public Biotech & Health comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) with a median P/S multiple of 6.6x.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $141M raised proxy, implying a $268M valuation. Peer-Median references the four same-sector peers, yielding a $3.5B median with a range from $539M to $10.3B. Public-Comp Anchoring cannot be applied due to lack of revenue data. The peer median reflects material dispersion: the $539M floor (Eikon Therapeutics, Series B) and $10.3B ceiling (Colossal, Series C) suggest stage and company-specific factors drive wide outcome variance.\n\nTriangulating these two methods yields a range of $228M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The wide spread reflects structural uncertainty: early-stage biotech valuations depend heavily on development stage, pipeline composition, and technical differentiation\u2014none fully captured in stage and sector filters alone. The peer median of $3.5B anchors the upper-middle portion of this range; the stage-progression method anchors the lower end. Without disclosed financial metrics or clinical-stage granularity, the $1.9B median should be treated as indicative rather than definitive.",
