      "narrative": "Nearfield Instruments, a Series D semiconductors company founded by Roland van Vliet and Hamed Sadeghian, has raised $147.6M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 3 public semiconductors players (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in the chips sector at similar or adjacent stages, including Tenstorrent, Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, and PsiQuantum.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $1.6B total-raised proxy, implying $2.4B. Peer-median valuation across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Etched ($5.0B, Series C), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014yields a median of $2.4B, with a range of $529M to $5.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples is not applicable because Nearfield's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $2.0B (low) to $2.8B (high), with a median of $2.4B. Both applicable methods converge tightly at this midpoint. Key uncertainties center on revenue scale and trajectory relative to the peer cohort, which exhibits substantial dispersion ($5.0B maximum versus $529M minimum), and the timing and terms of subsequent funding.",
