      "narrative": "Synspective is a publicly traded space and aerospace company founded by Motoyuki Arai that has raised approximately $220M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a peer set of four same-stage, same-sector comparables: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method, the sole applicable triangulation approach, yields an implied valuation of $5.2B. This represents the median across the four public space and aerospace peers identified. The wide dispersion within this peer set\u2014ranging from $840M at the low end to $40.0B at the high end\u2014reflects meaningful differences in technology focus, revenue scale, or market positioning within the sector, though specific underlying drivers are not detailed in the available data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.4B to $6.0B, with a median estimate of $5.2B. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data, which prevents application of revenue-multiple methodologies, and the substantial heterogeneity among public comparables, which limits confidence in the peer-median anchor. A revenue-adjusted assessment using the sector median P/S multiple of 27.4x would refine the estimate materially, conditional on disclosure of Synspective's top-line figures.",
