      "narrative": "Axelspace, a Series D\u2013stage space and aerospace company, is valued here through reference to a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B, Series D), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across these four comparables is $1.9B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring, though theoretically applicable to Space & Aerospace (which trades at a 27.4x P/S median across 6 public tickers including RKLB, PL, and LUNR), cannot be applied here because Axelspace's revenue is not publicly disclosed. The absence of revenue data precludes meaningful multiple-based valuation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.6B to $2.2B, centered on the $1.9B peer median. This range reflects valuation clustering among Series D peers (Apex Space at $2.3B and Varda at $1.6B) while acknowledging the wider dispersion created by earlier-stage comparables. Key uncertainty stems from the modest peer sample size (n=4) and the substantial outlier in Sierra Space at $8.0B, which widens confidence intervals. Revenue visibility for Axelspace would enable public-comp triangulation and tighter valuation banding.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-08-16T10:17:26+00:00"
