      "narrative": "ABL Bio is a public-listed biotech company on KOSDAQ within the Biotech & Health sector, which comprises 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 7 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nStandard triangulation methods encounter material constraints. Peer-median valuation is inapplicable: while 7 same-sector peers exist, none meet narrow filters for stage, adjacency, or valuation tier, leaving fewer than the required 3 datapoints for statistical reliability. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples is similarly blocked. The median P/S across the 3 public Biotech & Health comps is 6.6x; however, ABL Bio's revenue is not disclosed, precluding direct multiple application. The absence of revenue data reflects standard practice in life-sciences companies where valuation often hinges on pipeline stage, IP position, and financing rounds rather than near-term sales.\n\nWithout applicable quantitative methods, this analysis cannot derive a supported valuation range. A complete assessment would require either: ABL Bio's revenue disclosure to enable public-comp multiples, or sufficient same-stage private peer data with disclosed valuations to establish peer medians. Key uncertainties center on licensing revenue recognition (ABL Bio has raised $5B+ through licensing), pipeline advancement stage, and comparable company selection within the heterogeneous biotech universe.",
