      "narrative": "Constellr, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Max Gulde and Marius Bierdel, has raised \u20ac37M to date. The valuation landscape includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, though a sufficiently narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier does not exist to support median-based triangulation.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the primary applicable approach. Using total raised (\u20ac37M) as a value proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of \u20ac74M. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue. Peer-median methodology is not applicable; while 14 same-sector peers exist, the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar-tier) returned insufficient datapoints (0, 2, and 0 respectively) to support a robust median.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac63M\u2013\u20ac85M, centered on \u20ac74M. This reflects stage-typical progression but carries elevated uncertainty given reliance on a single method and the absence of revenue visibility. Key sensitivities include actual revenue run-rate (which would enable public-comp anchoring against the 27.4x P/S median in Space & Aerospace) and the availability of closer private peer comparables at Series A close. Resolution of either would tighten the range materially.",
