      "narrative": "Mimic Robotics is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $16M to date. The sector comprises 9 private peers (including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics) and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ), though the narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier is limited.\n\nGiven data constraints, valuation relies on the Stage-Progression method, which applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement. Using the $16M raised as a proxy baseline, this method implies a valuation of $40M. A peer-median approach was not executable; while 10 robotics sector peers exist, insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables (fewer than 3 datapoints after filtering) preclude reliable benchmarking.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $34M to $46M, centered on $40M median. Key uncertainties include the absence of same-stage peer density for triangulation and reliance on a single methodological approach. Any refinement would benefit from additional early-stage robotics comparable transactions or clearer visibility into unit economics and deployment traction. The range reflects stage-typical dilution assumptions but should be stress-tested against capital efficiency and market adoption timelines as additional data emerges.",
