      "narrative": "Vyoma is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac15M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 6 public space and aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE, though the latter set lacks sufficient granularity at Vyoma's stage and valuation tier for direct peer-median benchmarking.\n\nOf the three triangulation methods evaluated, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using the \u20ac15M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to Series B progression, the method implies a valuation of \u20ac30M. A peer-median approach could not be executed because of insufficient comparable data points at the same stage and similar scale within the Space & Aerospace sector. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples was similarly blocked by the absence of revenue disclosure for the private target.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac26M to \u20ac34M, with a median of \u20ac30M. This range reflects modest variance assumptions around the single applicable methodology. Key uncertainties include Vyoma's actual revenue run-rate (which would enable public-comp triangulation), the timing and structure of Series B fundraising, and competitive positioning relative to the underdisclosed private peer cohort. The narrow methodological base warrants treating this estimate as directional rather than definitive.",
