      "narrative": "Orbem is a Series B biotech and health company founded by Pedro G\u00f3mez, Maria Laparidou, and Miguel Molina Romero, having raised \u20ac55.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a private comparable universe of 8 companies in the same sector and stage, supplemented by 3 public biotech peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yields $105M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Colossal Biosciences at $10.3B, Chai Discovery at $3.8B, New Limit at $3.1B, and Eikon Therapeutics at $539M) produces a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 6.6x across the three public tickers) could not be applied due to absence of revenue data, typical for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods supports a valuation range of $90M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage-of-commercialization, capital efficiency relative to peers, and stage-specific risk. Stage-progression yields the conservative bound, while peer-median reflects the broader market context for late-stage private biotech.",
