      "narrative": "Kneron is a Series B chip design company in the Semiconductors sector, having raised $190M to date. The valuation analysis employs two applicable triangulation methods against a peer universe of 8 private and 3 public comparables in the same sector.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $190M raised proxy, implying $361M valuation. The Peer-Median method anchors to five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), Etched ($5.0B, Series C), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014yielding a median of $2.0B with a range of $529M to $11.0B. Public-Comp Anchoring across Semiconductors (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $307M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B. Stage-Progression yields the conservative bound, while Peer-Median anchors the upper range. Key uncertainties include Kneron's revenue scale and path to profitability relative to the peer cohort, which spans three consecutive stages and exhibits substantial dispersion ($529M to $11.0B). The wide peer range reflects sector-wide heterogeneity in commercialization maturity and capital efficiency.",
