      "narrative": "Asterra is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Lauren Guy that has raised $20M+ to date. The valuation landscape for early-stage space ventures is populated by 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables for reliable median pricing.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the applicable triangulation approach. Using total raised of $20M as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage step-ups yields an implied value of $40M. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 27.4x across the 6-ticker space sector universe) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures, which remain unavailable for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $34M to $46M, with a $40M median. This range reflects modest upside from capital raised, consistent with standard Series A progression mechanics. Primary uncertainties include the absence of granular revenue data (which would unlock public-comp validation) and the thinness of exact-stage private comparables in the space sector. Any higher valuation would require evidence of revenue trajectory or customer traction not present in available data.",
