      "narrative": "Mitra Chem is a Series B climate and energy technology company that has raised $60M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Lanzatech, ticker LNZA) in the same sector and development stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. The stage-progression method uses the $60M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a valuation of $114M. The peer-median method examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014KoBold Metals ($3.0B, Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B, Series C), and Amogy ($700M, Series C)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.0B and a range of $700M to $3.0B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneous risk profiles and technology maturity within the peer cohort.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a low estimate of $97M, a median of $557M, and a high of $1.1B. The significant spread reflects material uncertainty: the stage-progression method suggests earlier-stage valuation anchoring, while peer comparables are dominated by more advanced Series C companies with higher risk-adjusted valuations. Key sensitivities include technology differentiation relative to peers, path to commercialization, and capital efficiency relative to stage benchmarks. A tighter range would require more granular Series B-specific comparables or forward-looking financial metrics.",
