      "narrative": "Until, a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Laura Deming and Hunter Davis, has raised $106M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage biotech companies, though narrow peer matching constraints limit multi-method triangulation.\n\nOnly the Stage-Progression method applies with sufficient rigor. Using total raised ($106M) as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to the next financing stage yields an implied valuation of $212M. Peer-Median anchoring is not applicable: while 7 same-sector peers exist, filtering for identical stage, adjacent stage, and comparable valuation tier yields fewer than 3 datapoints, making sector-wide medians unreliable. Public-Comp Anchoring cannot be executed because Until's revenue is not on file; the public Biotech & Health median P/S multiple is 6.6x across the three tickers, but lacks a denominator.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $180M to $244M, with a central estimate of $212M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression point estimate. Key uncertainties include Until's actual revenue or revenue trajectory (needed for public-comp validation), the appropriate step-up multiplier for this specific cohort, and the relevance of the 8 private comparables given their limited public disclosure. A second-round financing or revenue visibility would materially improve valuation confidence.",
