      "narrative": "Sagence is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Vishal Sarin that has raised $58M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 8 private and 3 public comparables in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including SambaNova Systems ($11.0B Series A), Etched ($5.0B Series C), d-Matrix ($2.0B Series C), Positron AI ($1.0B Series B), and DEEPX ($529M Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement to the $58M raised proxy, yielding $110M. Peer-median analysis across the five same-sector comps produces a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures. The two methods produce materially different results, reflecting dispersion within the peer set and the inherent difficulty of timing valuation in early-stage semiconductor ventures.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $94M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.1B. The wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty around stage-specific comparables and the sensitivity of semiconductor valuations to technology differentiation and capital requirements. Key uncertainties include Sagence's specific technical positioning relative to peers, funding velocity, and macroeconomic conditions affecting the sector's exit multiples.",
