      "narrative": "LuxWall is a Series B-stage climate and energy company that has raised $84M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of nine private companies and one public peer (LNZA) in the climate and energy sector, including adjacent-stage Series C companies such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $84M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to next-stage advancement, yielding $160M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B and a range spanning $700M to $3.0B, implying $1.0B for LuxWall on a median-relative basis.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $136M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $580M. The wide dispersion between methods reflects material uncertainty around stage discount relative to Series C peers and the appropriate multiple to apply to early-stage raised capital. Key variables include LuxWall's revenue run-rate, capital efficiency trajectory relative to peer cohorts, and sector-level funding environment momentum in climate tech. Resolution of these factors will be critical to narrowing the range in subsequent rounds.",
