      "narrative": "AIM Intelligent Machines is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014alongside one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, anchoring to the $50M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, implies a $100M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the four-company robotics set yielded a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects stage heterogeneity within the peer set, with two Series B companies at the upper end and one Seed-stage company at the floor.\n\nThese methods support a triangulated range of $85M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $900M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median implies reflects both the early-stage nature of AIM relative to most sampled peers and uncertainty around the company's relative competitive positioning within the robotics sector. Key sensitivities include stage and timing of next financing, traction relative to Series B comparables, and whether peer valuations sustain in current market conditions.",
