      "narrative": "Fulfil is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Mir Aamir that has raised $127M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ), with the core peer set comprising Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Divergent, and Exotec.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses total capital raised ($127M) as a proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $241M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Generalist AI at $2.0B, Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, and Dexterity at $1.6B. The median across this cohort is $1.8B, establishing a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods produces a low estimate of $205M, a median of $996M, and a high of $2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material methodological differences: stage-progression anchors conservatively to deployment of capital, while peer-median reflects current market pricing for similar-stage robotics companies. Key uncertainties include whether Fulfil's operational metrics and market position align with the higher-valued peers in the comp set, and whether the stage-progression method appropriately captures risk-adjusted value for a Series B-stage business in a capital-intensive sector.",
