      "narrative": "Halo is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Andrei Iancu, Philip Van Stockum, and Charlie Rudy, having raised $122M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (SambaNova Systems, Etched, d-Matrix, Positron AI, DEEPX), supplemented by public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) for reference.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression uses the $122M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a $232M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 5-company sample yields a $2.0B valuation, reflecting the broad range inherent in early-stage semiconductor funding ($529M to $11.0B across the peer set). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 21.5x across three public tickers) cannot be applied without Halo's revenue figure, which is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range spans $197M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.1B. This wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Halo's technical progress, market traction, and competitive positioning relative to peers at varying stages. The gap between stage-progression ($232M) and peer-median ($2.0B) suggests valuation hinges critically on near-term execution milestones and product validation within the frontier semiconductor landscape.",
