      "narrative": "Alpha School, a Series A AI & Software company founded by MacKenzie Price and Brian Holtz, was valued using peer-median analysis against a universe of nine private and one public comparable (Palantir, ticker PLTR). The peer set includes Scale AI, Reflection AI, Physical Intelligence, and Black Forest Labs\u2014all same-sector, same or adjacent-stage companies\u2014yielding a median valuation of $15.3B across the four-company sample.\n\nPeer-median triangulation was the sole applicable method given available data. The four peers ranged from $3.2B (Black Forest Labs, Series B) to $29.0B (Scale AI, Series B), with Reflection AI (Series A) valued at $25.0B and Physical Intelligence (Series B) at $5.6B. This $3.2B\u2013$29.0B range reflects meaningful dispersion within the frontier-AI sector, attributable to differences in model maturity, capital efficiency, and market positioning. The $15.3B median serves as the point estimate.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $13.0B to $17.6B, centered on $15.3B. Key uncertainties include Alpha School's revenue traction, burn rate, and competitive positioning relative to the peer set\u2014variables not present in the current dataset. The single-method reliance and wide peer valuation dispersion (9x between min and max) introduce material estimation risk. Additional data on revenue, user growth, and capital deployed would sharpen the range.",
