      "narrative": "Compound Eye is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $20.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company operating in the same sector and stage, including three direct peers: Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $21M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-subsequent-stage advancement, yielding $39M. The peer-median method anchors on the three same-sector, same-stage comparables, which show a median valuation of $1.8B with a range of $1.6B\u2013$2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in robotics valuations at this stage, likely driven by differences in market maturity, deployment stage, and capital efficiency.\n\nTriangulation across both methods implies a valuation range of $33M to $2.0B, with a median of $895M. The substantial spread reflects the tension between intrinsic-stage metrics (stage progression) and peer-based relative valuation. The peer-median method dominates the upper bound given direct market comparables; however, execution risk, market traction, and competitive positioning relative to the three named peers remain critical uncertainties that would narrow this range in a full investment context.",
