      "narrative": "Star Catcher, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Andrew Rush, Michael Snyder, and Bryan Lyandvert, has raised $88M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 6 public players (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the only applicable method here. Using total capital raised ($88M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression yields $176M. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Star Catcher's revenue is not disclosed; the Space & Aerospace public median P/S of 27.4x across five tickers would require revenue visibility. Peer-median analysis is inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables in the narrow peer set\u2014only two adjacent-stage datapoints exist in the Space & Aerospace sector, below the three-company threshold for statistical reliability.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $150M to $202M, with a median point of $176M. This range reflects the single reliable method available. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data precluding P/S triangulation, limited publicly traded comparables in the frontier space sector, and stage-progression methodology's reliance on historical step-up patterns that may not capture Star Catcher's specific risk or growth profile. Additional diligence on unit economics and market timing would refine the estimate.",
