      "narrative": "Foundry Robotics is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Adarsh Kulkarni that has raised $19M to date. The valuation landscape for this sector includes one public comparable (277810.KQ) and eight private peers, including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable valuation framework. Using total capital raised of $19M as a baseline proxy and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the subsequent financing stage yields an implied valuation of $48M. This method is appropriate given the company's early stage, though peer-median analysis could not be applied due to insufficient data density\u2014the Robotics & Manufacturing universe contains only one same-stage comparable and no adjacent-stage or similar-tier private peers meeting the minimum threshold of three datapoints.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $40M to $55M, with a median point of $48M. This range reflects the 2.5x step-up assumption applied uniformly across the lower and upper bounds. Key uncertainties stem from the reliance on a single valuation methodology and the sparse peer set within the narrow sector-stage intersection. Further refinement would require either expanded comparable data or additional quantitative inputs such as revenue multiples, growth rates, or customer concentration metrics, none of which are available at this stage.",
