      "narrative": "Vector Defense, a Series A-stage defense and security company that has raised $61M to date, is valued against a comparable universe of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $122M. Peer-median methodology relies on three same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $400M, though the sample exhibits substantial dispersion\u2014ranging from $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). The peer-median implies $400M.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $104M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $261M. This wide distribution reflects meaningful uncertainty: the peer set's heterogeneity suggests stage and sector alone insufficiently capture company-specific risk, technology differentiation, or revenue trajectory. Vector Defense's specific revenue, unit economics, and customer concentration relative to named peers would narrow this range materially. The $104M\u2013$460M band is defensible on available data but should be refined through deeper operational diligence before pricing subsequent rounds.",
