      "narrative": "Lambda is a Series E AI & Software company that has raised $3.15B to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public (Palantir) and 8 private\u2014operating in the same sector at comparable or adjacent stages, including Applied Intuition, Wayve, SandboxAQ, and Ayar Labs.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses $3.1B in total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical of Series E advancement, yielding $4.4B. The peer-median method examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Applied Intuition ($15.0B, Series F), Wayve ($8.6B, Series D), SandboxAQ ($5.8B, Series E), and Ayar Labs ($3.8B, Series E). The resulting median is $7.2B, with a range of $3.8B to $15.0B.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a low estimate of $3.7B, a median of $5.8B, and a high of $8.3B. The median estimate of $5.8B aligns with the Series E peer cohort, though material uncertainty remains given the wide dispersion in peer valuations ($3.8B\u2013$15.0B) and the absence of disclosed recent fundraising terms for Lambda itself. Stage progression assumes standard step-ups; peer comparability depends on operational and market maturity alignment.",
