      "narrative": "Onebrief is a Series D defense and security technology company with a last post-money valuation of $2.1B and $336M in total raised. The company is evaluated against a comp universe of 10 peers: 8 private companies including Helsing, Saronic, and Chaos Industries, plus 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression modeling, anchored to the $2.1B Series D valuation and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for advancement to the next funding round, yields $3.2B. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage private companies\u2014Helsing ($18.0B), Saronic ($9.2B), and Chaos Industries ($4.5B)\u2014produces a median of $9.2B, with a range spanning $4.5B to $18.0B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $2.7B (low) to $10.6B (high), with a median of $6.2B. The current $2.1B valuation sits notably below the median, reflecting early Series D positioning. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven by differences in revenue scale, customer concentration, and defense-sector demand cycles\u2014and limited public market comps for precise discount rate calibration. The high end of the range should be treated as contingent on demonstrating revenue growth and customer traction consistent with top-quartile peers.",
