      "narrative": "DEFCON AI is a Seed-stage defense and security AI company founded by Yisroel Brumer, Paul Selva, and Grant Verstandig that has raised $44M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable set of 10 private companies and 2 public peers operating in the defense technology sector, including same-stage and adjacent-stage companies such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applied a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage transitions to the $44M raised as a proxy baseline, yielding $110M. Peer-median analysis across four comparable companies (Stark Defence at $4.0B, UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M) produced a median valuation of $700M, with a range of $125M to $4.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and scale differences within the peer set.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $94M to $805M, with a median of $405M. This wide band reflects two primary uncertainties: the substantial variance in peer valuations across the defense AI sector, and limited comparability between DEFCON AI's current Seed stage and the Series A-stage positioning of most peers. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer multiples drive the upper end. Additional clarity on revenue traction, customer commitments, and technical differentiation would narrow this range materially.",
