      "narrative": "Interlune is a seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by Rob Meyerson, Gary Lai, and Harrison Schmitt that has raised $23M to date. The sector comprises a fragmented peer universe of 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, though direct comparable benchmarking is constrained by heterogeneity and stage mismatch within the Space & Aerospace sector.\n\nPeer-median valuation proves inapplicable: the 14 same-sector peers identified do not yield sufficient datapoints meeting narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier combinations), falling short of the 3+ threshold required for reliable median estimation. Public-comp anchoring is similarly unavailable because Interlune, as a private company, does not disclose revenue\u2014precluding application of the sector P/S median of 27.4x observed across the 6-ticker public universe. Neither traditional triangulation method generates a defensible valuation range from the available data.\n\nAbsent disclosed revenue or a sufficiently dense peer set at matching stage and capital structure, this analysis cannot derive a quantitative valuation. Future work would require either (1) target revenue disclosure, (2) identification of seed-stage Space & Aerospace peers with known funding and valuations, or (3) alternative methodologies such as discounted cash flow grounded in disclosed business milestones. The $23M raised provides a cost basis but not a market valuation anchor.",
