      "narrative": "Sereact is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Ralf Gulde and Marc Tuscher that has raised $140M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three private companies at the same stage and sector (Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Generalist AI), supplemented by a broader universe of eight private robotics firms and one public comparable.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $266M. Peer-median analysis of same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014which valued at $1.6B, $1.8B, and $2.0B\u2014produces a median of $1.8B. The disparity reflects differences in company maturity, capital efficiency, and market positioning within the robotics sector.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $226M to $2.0B, with a median of $1.0B across both methods. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer multiples anchor the upper range. Key uncertainties include the revenue and margin profiles of peer companies, which substantively affect the relevance of their valuations; the pace and magnitude of customer adoption in manufacturing automation; and whether Sereact's technology differentiation commands a valuation premium or discount relative to comparables. A narrower range would require visibility into Sereact's revenue, unit economics, or customer pipeline relative to named peers.",
