      "narrative": "DG Matrix is a Series A climate and energy company founded by Haroon Inam and Subhashish Bhattacharya that has raised over $100M to date. The valuation universe comprises 9 same-sector peers, including 1 public company (LNZA) and 8 private firms such as Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. However, the peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables\u2014fewer than three datapoints survive stage and tier filtering\u2014limiting the applicability of median peer multiples.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression valuation is the primary applicable method. Using total capital raised ($100M) as a baseline value proxy and applying a standard 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to the subsequent financing stage yields an implied valuation of $200M. This approach assumes DG Matrix will command typical geometric growth between rounds, consistent with frontier energy and materials companies of comparable funding velocity.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $170M to $230M, centered on $200M median. The range reflects uncertainty inherent in single-method reliance and the absence of tight peer comparables at identical stage and valuation tier. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to broader Climate & Energy cohort and whether the company's technology differentiation and market traction support premium positioning within its peer universe. Validation would benefit from tighter comparable sets and granular performance metrics.",
