      "narrative": "Portal Biotech is a Series A biotech company founded by Andy Heron and Giovanni Maglia that has raised $35M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public peers in Biotech & Health (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private comparables including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable given data constraints. Stage-Progression analysis uses the $35M total raised as a proxy for pre-round valuation and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage step-ups, yielding an implied valuation of $70M. The Peer-Median approach could not be applied: while 7 biotech peers exist in the dataset, filtering by same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier yielded fewer than 3 comparable datapoints. Public-Comp Anchoring was also inapplicable because Portal Biotech's revenue is not on file\u2014a common constraint in private company valuation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $60M to $80M, with a median point estimate of $70M. This range reflects modest conservatism around the stage-progression baseline given the limited methodological triangulation. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue disclosure, which prevents revenue multiple calibration against the 6.6x median P/S observed in public biotech comps, and the lack of sufficiently dense private peer data for cross-validation. Investors should supplement this analysis with operational due diligence on Portal's pipeline and burn rate.",
