      "narrative": "Nudge is a Series A biotech company led by Fred Ehrsam (Coinbase co-founder), Quintin Frerichs, and Jeremy Barenholtz (ex-Neuralink VP). The company has raised $100M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public biotech & health peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the stage-progression method is reliably applicable. Using total raised ($100M) as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression yields $200M. Peer-median triangulation is not feasible: while 7 same-sector peers exist, none satisfy narrow filters for stage, adjacency, and valuation tier simultaneously. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 6.6x across the three biotech tickers) cannot be applied because Nudge's revenue is not disclosed\u2014standard for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $170M to $230M, with a median estimate of $200M. This range reflects the stage-progression methodology applied to available funding data. Key uncertainties include the lack of revenue visibility (precluding multiples-based methods), sparse near-peer data at the same stage, and the absence of disclosed financial metrics. Investors should treat this range as indicative pending access to internal financial performance and clearer peer comparability.",
