      "narrative": "Paradromics is a Series B biotech company founded by Matt Angle, with co-founders Edmund Huber and Andreas Schaefer. The company has raised approximately $90\u2013120M in dilutive capital plus ~$18M in non-dilutive NIH/DARPA funding. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Eikon Therapeutics, Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit) and 3 public biotech benchmarks (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $90M total raised proxy and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $171M. Peer-median analysis across the 4-company cohort yields $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M (Eikon Therapeutics) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as Paradromics does not publicly disclose revenue. The three public biotech comparables carry a median price-to-sales multiple of 6.6x, but this remains inapplicable absent the target's revenue figure.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $145M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B across the two applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around the company's clinical/commercial inflection point and the stage heterogeneity within the peer set (three Series C valuations vs. one Series B). Capital efficiency and pipeline advancement remain the primary drivers of upside or downside variance within this band.",
