      "narrative": "Groq is a Series C-stage semiconductor company founded by Jonathan Ross and Douglas Wightman that has raised $3.0B to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public semiconductors (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private frontier-chip firms, with immediate peers including Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and DEEPX ($529M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression anchors to total capital raised ($3.0B) and applies a typical Series C step-up multiplier of 1.7x, implying a valuation of $5.1B. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comps yields a median of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Groq's revenue is not disclosed, which is standard for private companies. The public semiconductors universe trades at a 21.5x median P/S (across ALAB, NVDA, AMD), but application requires revenue data.\n\nTriangulating these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $1.7B (low) to $5.9B (high), with a median of $3.5B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Groq's competitive positioning relative to specialized chip peers and revenue trajectory. The stage-progression method suggests upside to $5.1B, while peer-median anchors more conservatively at $2.0B. Key uncertainties include Groq's unreported revenue and whether its market position warrants a premium or discount to the three-peer median.",
