      "narrative": "Oishii, a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Hiroki Koga and Brendan Somerville, has raised $386M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company in the robotics sector, with primary focus on 3 same-stage private peers: Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total capital raised ($386M) as a proxy for entry valuation, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $656M. The peer-median approach anchors to the median valuation of the 3-company same-sector, same-stage cohort at $1.0B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B across the sample.\n\nThese methods support a triangulated valuation range of $557M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $828M. The dispersion between methods\u2014$399M between low and high\u2014reflects meaningful uncertainty around both Oishii's relative market position within the peer set and the appropriate step-up multiple for this stage. Key unknowns include specific revenue and growth metrics relative to comps, and whether Oishii's technology differentiation or market timing justify positioning toward the upper or lower quartile of the peer range.",
