      "narrative": "XDOF, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Philipp Wu, Fred Shentu, and Nemo Jin, has raised $142M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public entity operating in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages, including peers such as Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this stage. Stage-progression analysis uses total capital raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $284M. Peer-median analysis examines four robotics companies at Series B and Seed stages, which traded at a median valuation of $1.7B (range: $1.1B\u2013$2.0B). This peer set reflects both earlier-stage reference points and more mature comparables within the sector.\n\nThese methods triangulate to a range of $241M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $992M. The wide dispersion reflects the stage heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014the inclusion of Series B valuations materially elevates the midpoint relative to stage-progression alone. Key uncertainties center on XDOF's revenue profile, unit economics, and go-to-market progress relative to the Series B comparables, which would materially inform positioning within this range. The $284M stage-progression result provides a floor reflecting current capital deployed, while the $1.7B peer median reflects market multiples being paid for later-stage robotics assets.",
