      "narrative": "nTop, a Series C robotics and manufacturing software company founded by Bradley Rothenberg and Greg Schroy, has raised $138.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014within the robotics and manufacturing sector, including stage-matched peers Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to nTop. The stage-progression approach, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $139M raised proxy, implies a valuation of $236M. The peer-median method, based on three same-stage robotics and manufacturing comparables, yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. The significant spread between these methods reflects differing assumptions about nTop's relative maturity and market position relative to named peers.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $201M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $618M. The wide dispersion\u2014driven principally by the gap between capital-efficiency assumptions (stage-progression) and peer-relative positioning (peer-median)\u2014underscores key uncertainties: nTop's revenue scale relative to Hadrian and peers, its customer concentration and retention, and whether its software-first positioning commands a premium or discount to hardware-integrated competitors. Additional revenue and profitability data would narrow this range materially.",
