      "narrative": "Viam, a Series C robotics and manufacturing platform founded by Eliot Horowitz, has raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company in the robotics sector, with primary focus on 3 same-stage private peers: Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yields $199M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $1.0B to $1.6B. The divergence between methods reflects the significant spread observed within the peer set.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $169M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $599M. The substantial width of this range reflects material uncertainty about how Viam's capital efficiency, market traction, and product positioning compare to documented peers. Key variables affecting placement within the range include revenue multiples relative to peers, customer concentration and retention metrics, and the pace of Series C deployment relative to comparable fundraises.",
