      "narrative": "Nitricity is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $102.8M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a comparable universe of three same-stage, same-sector private peers (Generalist AI at $2.0B, Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, and Dexterity at $1.6B), supplemented by a broader peer set of eight private companies and one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($103M) as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $195M. The peer-median method references the three identified stage and sector comparables, which display a median valuation of $1.8B with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B. This reflects valuations observed in the active robotics and manufacturing segment.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide implied range: $195M (stage-progression low) to $1.8B (peer-median center). The triangulated analysis supports a range of $166M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $973M. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the three-peer sample given the heterogeneity typical in robotics subsectors, and whether capital-raised multiples appropriately anchor early-stage positioning relative to current market comparables. The $807M spread between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects material ambiguity around appropriate valuation precedent.",
