      "narrative": "Privateer, a Series A space technology company founded by Steve Wozniak, Alex Fielding, and Moriba Jah, has raised $73.1M to date. The Space & Aerospace sector includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, though the private peer set remains fragmented across different stages and business models.\n\nOf three standard valuation methods, only stage-progression triangulation is applicable given data constraints. The stage-progression approach applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression to the $73.1M total raised, implying a $146M valuation. Peer-median comparison is not reliable: while 14 same-sector peers exist, filtering to relevant stage and valuation tiers yields fewer than three datapoints. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Privateer's revenue is not disclosed, precluding calculation of an EV/Sales multiple against the sector median of 27.4x across public Space & Aerospace names.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $124M to $168M, centered on a median of $146M. However, this reflects a single methodological anchor. Key uncertainties include Privateer's current revenue run rate, near-term growth profile, and differentiation within the crowded space infrastructure market. A second valuation method\u2014either peer-based once comparable financials are available, or revenue-based upon disclosure\u2014would materially strengthen conviction in this range.",
