      "narrative": "Electric Sheep, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Gunjit Singh, Jarrett Herold, and Naganand Murty, has raised $25.5M to date. Valuation analysis relies on two primary methods triangulated against a comparable universe of 4 private peers (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Walden Robotics) in the same sector and stage, supplemented by a broader set of 8 private robotics companies and 1 public comparable.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $25.5M total raised, yielding $51M. The Peer-Median method establishes a reference point from four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B), producing a median of $1.7B. The wide range reflects heterogeneity in peer staging and maturity within the robotics sector.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $43M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $876M. The 46x spread between low and high estimates reflects substantial uncertainty around Electric Sheep's competitive positioning relative to more mature Series B peers and the appropriate stage adjustment. Key variables driving valuation include demonstrated market traction, capital efficiency relative to peer burn rates, and the strength of differentiation in a crowded robotics landscape.",
