      "narrative": "Swarmbotics AI is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by Stephen Houghton and Drew Watson, which has raised $17.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 companies spanning public and private markets: 2 public peers (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private defense-tech firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies $43M. Peer-median analysis examined 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Stark Defence ($4.0B Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B Seed), Singularity ($400M Series A), and NODA AI ($125M Series A). The median valuation across this set is $700M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods yields a valuation range of $37M (low) to $805M (high), with a median estimate of $372M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around market positioning relative to the peer set. Key drivers of variance include whether Swarmbotics' technology and commercial trajectory align more closely with earlier-stage peers or with the higher-valuation Series A comparables, and the degree to which defense-sector dynamics command sector-specific premiums independent of stage progression.",
