      "narrative": "zeroRISC is a Seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Dominic Rizzo that has raised $15M to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector comprises 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched, though narrow peer matching at the Seed stage proved limited.\n\nOnly the Stage-Progression method proved applicable to this valuation. Using total capital raised ($15M) as a proxy for post-money Seed valuation and applying a standard 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $38M. The Peer-Median approach was inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables in the narrow peer universe\u2014while 12 total Chips & Semiconductors peers exist, fewer than 3 met valuation-tier or stage filters. Public-Comp Anchoring could not be deployed because zeroRISC's revenue is not on file, preventing use of the public sector's 21.5x median P/S multiple.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $32M to $43M (low to high), centered on $38M. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue disclosure, which precludes market-multiple triangulation, and the sparsity of same-stage private semiconductor comparables, which limits peer benchmarking. The single-method conclusion warrants sensitivity testing against alternative stage multipliers and validation through subsequent funding round outcomes.",
