      "narrative": "Argo Space is a Seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Robert, Ryan, and Kirby Carlisle that has raised $13.6M to date. The Space & Aerospace sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, though a tightly filtered peer set at identical stage and valuation tier remains insufficient for reliable median benchmarking.\n\nGiven data constraints, only stage-progression methodology applies here. Using total capital raised ($14M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next stage yields $34M. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 27.4x across the 6-ticker sector universe) cannot be deployed without disclosed revenue figures, which private companies typically do not publish. A narrow peer-median approach fails due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage datapoints within the Space & Aerospace cohort.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $29M to $39M, with a point estimate of $34M. This range reflects modest variance around a single applicable method rather than true triangulation across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include actual revenue run-rate and customer traction, which would enable public-comp validation; the absence of same-stage peer valuations limits confidence in the stage-progression assumption. Investors should treat this as a floor pending disclosure of operational metrics.",
