      "narrative": "Danti, a seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Jesse Kallman and Martice Nicks III, has raised $10.9M to date. The valuation universe consists of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, though narrow same-stage filtering yields insufficient data for traditional peer-median approaches.\n\nGiven limited comparable density at the seed stage within Space & Aerospace, the analysis relies on stage-progression methodology. Using the $10.9M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier standard for Seed-to-Series A progression yields $27.3M. The public comp universe trades at a median 27.4x P/S, but Danti's revenue remains undisclosed, precluding direct public-comp anchoring. The triangulated valuation range of $23M\u2013$31M reflects a \u00b115% band around the $27M stage-progression result.\n\nKey uncertainties include the absence of disclosed revenue (preventing P/S calibration against public peers), the lack of sufficient private seed-stage comparables with transaction data, and the broad heterogeneity within Space & Aerospace across launch, imaging, and infrastructure subsectors. The $27M median should be treated as indicative pending disclosure of financial metrics or evidence of revenue traction that would enable public-comp anchoring.",
