      "narrative": "Cognitive Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Guy de Carufel that has raised $10.3M to date. The valuation universe comprises 14 private peers in Space & Aerospace (including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs) alongside 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression triangulation was applicable. Using total capital raised ($10.3M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the next financing stage yields an implied valuation of $26M. Peer-median analysis could not be applied due to insufficient datapoints within narrow stage and tier filters\u2014while 14 same-sector peers exist, none met minimum cohort size requirements (\u22653 matches). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 27.4x across the five traded comparables) could not be applied because the target's revenue is not on file, as is standard for undisclosed private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $22M to $30M, centered on $26M. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data (preventing revenue multiple validation), limited comparable transactional data at seed stage in the space sector, and the high-risk, capital-intensive nature of aerospace ventures. Investors should treat this range as preliminary pending disclosure of financial performance metrics.",
