      "narrative": "Gambit is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Josh Giegel, Ben Richardson, and Andrew Kemendo that has raised $6.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector and stage, including peer benchmarks like UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $6.5M total raised as a proxy valuation base and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage transitions, yielding $16M. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B Seed), Singularity ($400M Series A), and NODA AI ($125M Series A)\u2014producing a median valuation of $700M and a range of $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $14M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $358M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in early-stage defense-tech valuations, particularly given the significant spread across the peer set ($125M to $4.0B). Stage-progression implies conservative valuation; peer-median suggests substantially higher potential. Key uncertainties include product-market fit validation, customer concentration risk, and regulatory pathway clarity in defense applications.",
