      "narrative": "Ghost Robotics is a Seed-stage defense and security robotics company founded by Avik De, Jiren Parikh, and Gavin Kenneally. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector and stage cohort, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the company's $1.85M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression, implying a $5M valuation. The Peer-Median method benchmarks against four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Stark Defence at $4.0B, UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M), yielding a median valuation of $700M with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $4M to $805M, with a median estimate of $352M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Ghost Robotics' competitive positioning within a highly fragmented defense tech market and the significant variance in peer valuations across the comp set. Stage-Progression and peer benchmarking diverge substantially, suggesting that isolated comps metrics are insufficient without additional visibility into the company's product maturity, customer traction, and defensibility relative to the peer group.",
